&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;The Strategic Pursuits team is a new group within Stripe’s Enterprise Platform Sales&amp;nbsp;organization, built to win Stripe’s most complex and high-impact opportunities. This team focuses&amp;nbsp;on multi-year, transformative sales cycles with the world’s largest software platforms and&amp;nbsp;enterprises—companies that have the potential to fundamentally shift Stripe’s presence in new&amp;nbsp;industries and markets.&amp;nbsp;Strategic Pursuits is responsible for identifying, shaping, and closing Stripe’s most significant&amp;nbsp;platform partnerships. These are long, intricate engagements requiring deep collaboration across&amp;nbsp;executive, product, and engineering teams and the ability to influence strategic priorities on both&amp;nbsp;sides of the table. The team’s work often extends well beyond payments, helping partners&amp;nbsp;co-develop entirely new business models and revenue streams powered by Stripe’s financial&amp;nbsp;infrastructure stack, including Connect, Billing, Payments, and Banking as a Service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;As an Account Executive, Strategic Pursuits , you will lead the end-to-end pursuit of Stripe’s&amp;nbsp;largest and most complex platform opportunities. You’ll act as both strategist and dealleader—identifying transformative prospects, crafting multi-year engagement plans, and&amp;nbsp;orchestrating resources across Stripe to bring highly tailored solutions to market. This is a senior,&amp;nbsp;cross-functional sales role that combines strategic vision, financial acumen, and strong technical&amp;nbsp;understanding with world-class relationship management.&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;● &lt;/span&gt;Lead the pursuit of Stripe’s most complex and high-value enterprise platform&amp;nbsp;opportunities, from initial identification through negotiation and close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;● &lt;/span&gt;Develop a multi-year strategic plan for each pursuit account, grounded in a deep&amp;nbsp;understanding of the customer’s business model, technical architecture, and market&amp;nbsp;opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;● &lt;/span&gt;Build trusted relationships with executive stakeholders across business, finance, product,&amp;nbsp;and engineering—both internally and within prospective client organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;● &lt;/span&gt;Collaborate closely with Product, Solutions Architecture, Deal Pricing, Engineering,&amp;nbsp;Finance, and Legal to design bespoke commercial and technical solutions that extend&amp;nbsp;beyond payments and unlock new growth for both Stripe and the customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;● &lt;/span&gt;Lead cross-functional deal teams , driving alignment on strategy, scope, and resourcing&amp;nbsp;to ensure the successful execution of pursuit plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;● &lt;/span&gt;Serve as the executive point of contact for the customer, guiding complex discussions&amp;nbsp;around value realization, integration design, and long-term partnership potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;● &lt;/span&gt;Partner with Stripe leadership to shape go-to-market strategy in new industries and&amp;nbsp;verticals informed by insights from these strategic opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;● &lt;/span&gt;Represent the customer’s voice internally, influencing Stripe’s product roadmap and&amp;nbsp;commercial strategy based on the needs of the largest, most sophisticated platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;You are a seasoned enterprise seller and strategic operator who thrives in high-stakes,&amp;nbsp;ambiguous environments. You are comfortable leading large, cross-functional pursuits that&amp;nbsp;require creativity, patience, and precision. You combine deep financial and technical&amp;nbsp;understanding with exceptional executive presence and storytelling. You’re equally adept at&amp;nbsp;designing commercial frameworks, navigating complex organizational dynamics, and inspiring&amp;nbsp;teams toward shared outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;● &lt;/span&gt;10+ years of enterprise sales or business development experience, ideally within fintech,&amp;nbsp;payments, or SaaS infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;● &lt;/span&gt;Proven success leading multi-year, multi-stakeholder enterprise sales cycles with&amp;nbsp;contract values in the 7–8 figure range.&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;● &lt;/span&gt;Demonstrated ability to orchestrate large internal deal teams , aligning across product,&amp;nbsp;legal, and finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;● &lt;/span&gt;Exceptional executive communication skills with experience presenting to and negotiating&amp;nbsp;with C-level leaders (CTO, CFO, COO) .&lt;/p&gt;
