&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Support team directly supports our largest and fastest growing users, partnering with them to grow their business. We actively seek and capitalize on opportunities to meet and exceed their service expectations, working to impress the trendsetters and remove obstacles from their path. The team is there when users need us but also there proactively - before they even realize they need support. The Critical Support&amp;nbsp; team exists within Product Support to help address the most escalated user issues. This team responds to users who have sent their issue or concerns to a member of their Stripe account team or to a Stripe executive. We own the resolution of the immediate issue at hand, as well as ensuring that the factors that led to the escalation are addressed and remediated.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ultimately, these cases often shine a light on points of failures within Stripe, and the team has the opportunity to create transformative user experiences, while also helping edit Stripe to rectify the structural issues that resulted in the escalation in the first place.&amp;nbsp;This is a high visibility, high impact role, with the responsibility to work with executives users and cross functional stakeholders, all while helping shape the evolution of this team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a strategic leader to continue to build and lead Critical Support as Stripe’s ultimate.&amp;nbsp; You will own the strategy, operating model, and cross-functional partnerships that enable Stripe to resolve the most severe and consequential user issues with urgency, judgment, and lasting impact on Stripe’s product and processes.&amp;nbsp; You will equally wear a strategic and operational hat.&amp;nbsp; You&amp;nbsp; will lead a high performing team of escalations specialists to deliver exceptional user experiences. This team goes beyond basic troubleshooting—it&#39;s about&amp;nbsp; developing a team of product and process expertise with analytical mindset and project management skills to strategically improve our support systems, processes, and product quality. You will play a key role to cultivate the happiness of their team through clear goal setting, feedback mechanism, mentoring, and advocacy within the organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the organization to design and deliver scalable user support by partnering effectively with cross functional stakeholders across Product, Engineering and broader teams such Sales (Go-To-Market), Risk etc as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-own &amp;amp; drive Critical Support strategy, operating model, and multi-quarter roadmap development that meets or exceeds Stripe’s users and internal stakeholders expectations towards critical support experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted partner to Sales, Account Management, Product, Engineering, Risk, and executive leadership during high-stakes user situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive strong operational delivery and process improvement helping to mitigate risk while balancing operational efficiency and user impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain metrics and analysis of team performance, and provide regular reporting on team performance in the form of written analysis and performance reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong ties with cross-functional teams and position the Critical Support team to act as ultimate unblocking force for users as well as source of the insights on Stripe’s product and process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear goals and directions, and provide regular feedback on team members’ performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure team members are happy, effective, and growing in their career and new work experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transmit and foster our values, serving as a beacon of Stripe’s user-centric philosophy and culture of transparency, empathy, inclusion, and empowerment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build the organization through management projects such as recruiting, training, writing team policies, defining team processes, or other organizational improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 8+ years of direct people management experience; including senior front line specialists and/or managers and supported them to career growth and transitions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading operational teams such as product support teams (preferably in high-growth technology companies)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in strategizing and driving large scale operational process improvements and program management work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience in stakeholder management, with the ability to influence cross-functional teams and drive progress for the team and users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical sense and track-record of making data driven decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skill and credibility doing the core work of a user facing team with a high bar for quality and a willingness to lead by example and get into the details of front-line work if required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership mindset and experience in driving highly complex initiatives at speed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with Escalations, Incident Management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with some technical troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with FinTech industry and products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for learning new functions and features of technical products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Critical Support Operations Associate, Weekend Coverage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Critical Support team is Stripe&#39;s frontline response function for urgent, high-stakes user issues. We operate at the intersection of hands-on support execution, incident response, and cross-functional coordination. Our mandate is to protect users in their most business-critical moments—resolving executive-triggered escalations, urgent and critical-priority cases, and complex issues that require more than a standard resolution path. We work closely with Internal Risk Management, Product, Engineering, and Legal to drive fast, coordinated outcomes. This is a greenfield team: we are building the operational foundations, workflows, and standards that will define critical support at Stripe for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Critical Support OA, you will be the first operational responder on Stripe&#39;s most urgent and time-sensitive user issues. You will execute against escalation cases across a wide range of complex scenarios—from executive-triggered requests and critical payment failures to urgent user escalations requiring immediate cross-functional coordination. This is a builder role: in addition to resolving cases, you will actively help shape the processes, playbooks, and operational standards that make this team function. You will develop a strong foundation in executive communication, complex problem-solving under pressure, and operational execution in an ambiguous, high-stakes environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; Operation Associates in this role will work either Saturday to Wednesday, or Wednesday to Sunday.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Case Execution: Handle escalation cases (Executive Escalations, User Escalations, urgent@/critical@) with speed and sound judgment, ensuring users in business-critical situations receive timely, high-quality support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide consistent, reliable coverage for our business critical support flows (urgent@ and critical@).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Coordination: Engage proactively with Incident Management, Risk, Product, Engineering, and other internal partners to drive resolution for complex issues that span multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder Communication: Communicate clearly and professionally with senior internal stakeholders and high-profile external users, distilling complex situations into concise updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process Building: Contribute actively to defining and documenting operational workflows, escalation criteria, and resolution playbooks as the team establishes its foundations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Queue Operations: Support Escalations queue duties during non-shift time, including triage and review of ongoing escalation cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous Improvement: Identify patterns in case volume and resolution paths, surfacing actionable insights to improve team workflows and reduce recurring friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completed secondary education or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 2 years of professional experience within Payments, Fintech, or SaaS support environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to cover Weekends consistency e.g. Saturday - Wednesday or Wednesday - Sunday.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency: you operate with independence, take ownership of outcomes, and don&#39;t wait to be told what to do next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stay composed and exercise sound judgment in high-pressure, ambiguous situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to adjust tone and level of detail for different audiences, including senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative approach to problem-solving—you know when to escalate, when to coordinate, and when to drive toward a decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine user empathy paired with a drive to fix root causes, not just close tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in payments, fintech, or SaaS support environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completed secondary education or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI Fluency: You have experience working with agentic workflows, prompting and iteration. You understand how to assess output quality and apply critical thinking in AI usage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling executive-level or executive-triggered support cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with incident management, SFDC or case management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated interest in building operational programs—process documentation, workflow design, or cross-functional project work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Financial Crimes Compliance Risk Oversight (FinCRO) is hiring an Enterprise Compliance and Risk Controls Lead for financial crimes controls and governance at Stripe. This role will support Bridge and Privy controls plus provide critical inputs for policy governance and Financial Crimes Risk Assessment (FCRA) across Stripe entities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will combine financial crimes controls expertise with strong program management, using AI responsibly to improve the quality, consistency, and scalability of our work. The role will support key financial crimes priorities, including evolving requirements related to the Travel Rule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Bridge and Privy controls are appropriately designed, evidenced, governed, and implemented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive relevant financial crimes policy governance across Stripe entities, including policy development, approvals, and change management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide critical inputs for the Financial Crimes Risk Assessment across Stripe entities, including planning, stakeholder coordination, documentation, governance, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate financial crimes regulatory and risk requirements into clear, practical controls, policies, risk assessments, and operating processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Financial Crimes, Compliance, Legal, Risk, Product, Engineering, Operations, and Internal Audit to identify gaps, manage issues, and improve the control environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify responsible AI and automation opportunities across controls, policy, and risk-assessment work including document review, obligation mapping, evidence triage, change analysis, and trend reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure AI-enabled workflows retain appropriate human oversight, data protection, accountability, and auditability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in financial crimes compliance, risk, internal controls, audit, or a related field in regulated financial services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with financial crimes risk assessments, control design or testing, policy governance, issue management, or audit readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with financial crimes requirements, ideally including AML, sanctions, KYC/KYB, transaction monitoring, and/or the Travel Rule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in or experience using AI and automation to improve compliance, controls, risk, or operational workflows responsibly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Accounting Team is responsible for supporting all products at Stripe, consulting on accounting implications, and supporting teams&#39; ability to make informed strategic decisions. We are responsible for the accurate and timely recording of all business-generated transactions on our balance sheet and income statement. We operate in a fast-paced environment and collaborate significantly with cross-functional and international teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is seeking an experienced accountant to join our world-class accounting team. In this role, you will support revenue and cost accounting for products developed by our Bridge subsidiary, leveraging your technical expertise with U.S. GAAP, specifically ASC 606, to quickly identify accounting implications and impacts on customers while advising and collaborating with team members cross-functionally to develop operational processes that help us scale. Ideally, you will have both public accounting and industry experience in tech or financial services, as well as experience working for companies with a high volume of complex transactions and issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own P&amp;amp;L accounting for Bridge&#39;s products, including journal entries, reconciliations, variance analyses, financial reporting deliverables, and analytical reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Bridge&#39;s product, go-to-market, and finance partners to thoroughly understand new products, features, and contracts, and advise on accounting implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal systems and engineering teams to support internal financial systems and automation of accounting processes, and identify, recommend, and implement scalable accounting processes to support global growth at Bridge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and prepare technical accounting analyses, assess the effectiveness of internal controls, and design new processes and controls for emerging and growing business activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand data and system flows, analyze financial results to identify and address anomalies, and support external audit processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant public accounting or industry experience, with a B.A. or B.S. degree in Accounting or Finance (CPA strongly preferred), experience accounting for cryptocurrencies including stablecoins, and experience with SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in U.S. GAAP and ability to research complex accounting issues, with a proven track record of managing high volumes of complex transactions and financial issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills with the ability to convey financial concepts to both financial and non-financial audiences, and demonstrated success working collaboratively and influencing cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated history of taking on challenging projects and producing results with excellent attention to detail, and a solution-oriented mindset with enthusiasm for establishing best practices and challenging existing processes to identify improvement opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of or experience in the technology or payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Bridge&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Stripe company, Bridge develops a fully integrated stablecoin platform to enable global money movement and operates as a Luxembourg-regulated Electronic Money Institution (EMI) and Crypto-Asset Service Provider (CASP). Organizations partner with Bridge to receive, store, convert, issue, and spend stablecoins, which allows them to expand into new markets, deploy innovative products, and transfer funds with greater speed and efficiency. Stripe provides the underlying financial infrastructure for these operations, supporting millions of businesses worldwide—ranging from global enterprises to high-growth startups—in accepting payments, increasing revenue, and capturing new commercial opportunities. Driven by a shared mission to grow the internet&#39;s GDP, we have a significant workload ahead. This offers you an opportunity to help expand access to the global economy while engaging in impactful work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At BBSA, money movement is central, and the Customer Fund Reconciliation Manager plays a vital role in verifying that daily fund transfers across wallets and bank accounts are fully reconciled. As Bridge and Stripe develop an automated end-to-end reconciliation system, you assist the team in refining the workflow, adapting it to incorporate new product rollouts, investigating daily discrepancies, and analyzing unreconciled items to determine next steps. You use strong problem-solving skills to provide leadership with clear, precise summaries of daily reconciliation rates, highlight the primary drivers of discrepancies, and identify areas that require further review. Rather than a standard month-end controllership position, this is a technical operational role focused heavily on data analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You collaborate with the Reconciliation product team in New York while directly supporting BBSA’s management group in Luxembourg. This position is located in Luxembourg.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the complete end-to-end automated reconciliation system from a technical and engineering standpoint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and execute the daily investigation of unreconciled BBSA transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and submit daily reconciliation status updates to the authorized management team at BBSA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the continuous optimization of the Reconciliation platform by converting operational insights into clear remediation plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confirm that the automated end-to-end reconciliation workflow fully integrates all newly introduced BBSA products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present reconciliation findings and strategic recommendations to senior leadership and external bodies, including the Board, Audit Committee, and CSSF&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking candidates who meet the core requirements for this position. If you meet these criteria, we look forward to your application. Note that preferred qualifications are an added asset, not a mandatory prerequisite.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in payment operations and reconciliations, including experience working with international companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL skills and comfort working across systems and handling large volumes of data. A live SQL assessment is part of the interview process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of accounting principles, banking systems, and data structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with engineers and accounting teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High professional fluency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EMI or PI experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of blockchain and data structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working for a US company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our users are the heart of our business. Stripe’s Global Customer Success Team is responsible for managing our largest and most strategic relationships, such as Bytedance, Canva, and Shopify. In this manager role you’ll be responsible for a high-performing team of Customer Success Managers covering the Greater China Region. You’ll lead and coach the team, helping them deliver on ambitious targets, as well as roll up your sleeves to work directly with executives at existing enterprise Stripe customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a self-starter who has demonstrated success dealing with ambiguity, operating in a high-growth environment, and solving complicated problems with limited oversight. Ideal candidates will have management and leadership experience scaling a technology sales or account management team, superior communication skills, and a knack for understanding unique customer needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Manager to lead a team of high-performing Customer Success Managers to build and grow the relationships with our most complex users from the Greater China region.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
