&lt;p&gt;Global Business Services’ (GBS) primary goal is to ensure operational excellence across deal cycles, increase revenue through the development of transformative commercial constructs, and drive closure of Stripe’s sold portfolio. The team&#39;s reach is widespread across Stripe, not exclusive to one sales segment or geographical region. GBS drives change across go-to-market, positively impacting Stripe users and cross-functional teams. GBS priorities are set through the direction of Stripe leadership and executive vision, partnership with sales and cross-functional organizations, as well as user feedback and market insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Business Services (GBS) team is looking for a Deal Strategist to focus on the closure of custom and standard commercial deals. You&#39;ll be responsible for deal lifecycle management and supporting cross-organizational alignment. This role requires a background in driving custom commercial and pricing deals to closure, a strong understanding of private pricing frameworks, as well as experience supporting sales through negotiations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have experience with subscription products, pricing strategies, and a background in supporting selling motions. You have strong communication skills. You&#39;ll love this job if you are a natural relationship and mechanism builder.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage end-to-end customer deals —drafting, editing, and reviewing agreements—while supporting the sales cycle to ensure deal terms align with business goals, reflect strategic priorities, and close as forecasted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary point of contact between Sales, Legal, and other cross-functional stakeholders for deal-related questions, approvals, and escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with sales teams, sales leaders, services/support teams and customers to advise on deal structures, establish compelling commercials, and drive closure of customer issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the business and technical requirements of our customers and partners, advising sales teams on the best approach (balancing risk between custom terms and internal system limitations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove internal blockers and drive solutions between cross-functional teams such as Product, Legal, Finance, Accounting, Service Teams, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial and legal agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the pricing and structuring of multithreaded product use cases in all segments and industries especially in highly competitive sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quickly build credibility and trust with internal customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strong support, communication, and persuasion skills including XFN and senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree in Business, Technology, Finance, or Economics with 8+ years of experience in deal management, procurement, pricing strategy, or financial consulting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in ambiguous, quickly scaling environments, comfortable with high-agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, presentation, negotiation, and project management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Payments and SaaS, and redlining agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Salesforce and Ironclad&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;AI fluency and passion for applying emerging technology efficiencies in the day-to-day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience training or enabling sales teams on pricing, quoting, and contract best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Web Presence and Platform is organized into two pillars, each of which is grouped into pods that focus on the central tenets of Stripe&#39;s public mission. The Presence pillar creates industry-leading designs for Stripe&#39;s front door surfaces, educating customers about the power of our platform, sharing Stripe&#39;s ideas and expertise with the public, and driving adoption. The Platform pillar builds the internal machinery that powers these surfaces, and is responsible for making our websites fast, stable, and easy to update.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together we design and build stripe.com and other sites that amount to what is, for many, their first impression of Stripe. As such, WPP offers exciting opportunities to have a major impact on Stripe&#39;s success. We want to make every pixel count, we want it to be enthralling, and we want to help other Stripes seamlessly benefit from our systematic work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Design Engineer you will concept, prototype, and build new experiences for our web presence. You&#39;ll bring your creativity and expertise to the full range of the Stripe brand, across evergreen pages as well as time-based campaigns. You&#39;ll both utilize and contribute to our libraries and design systems, and, when appropriate, work outside established systems to create new digital moments. You&#39;ll constantly have in-browser performance in mind, and create abstractions that other designers and engineers consume and build upon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All Design Engineers in WPP have a shared commitment to user experience and craft, but each pod has subtly different focus areas. The Collective pod leverages design, animation, and interaction to drive awareness, educate prospective users, and share Stripe&#39;s expertise across public surfaces such as Stripe.com, Link, and others. The Expansion pod brings the same creativity and executional rigor to attracting new prospects and driving conversion, focusing on user journeys, interactive and highly polished tools for users, and building targeted experiences for our global users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Design Engineer on the Collective pod, you will help us continue to drive Stripe.com forward, bringing new experiences to life or refining existing content to inform prospective users about the company and its offerings. You will partner closely with designers, other engineers, and partners to execute and evolve the site, bringing technical craft and creativity to the expansive scope of Stripe&#39;s web presence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with our team&#39;s designers and partners to both create new experiences for and maintain Stripe.com&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with other design engineers, pairing, mentoring, and continually building a culture of excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype and implement web animations and interaction-heavy product launch materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build beautiful, best-in-class end-user experiences to solve complex problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize, maintain, and extend our design systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate our web platform with self-serve authoring and experimentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of relevant web front-end development or creative technology experience at a tech-forward, product-driven company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced knowledge of modern HTML and CSS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing clear, elegant code in a team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A zeal for the web as a storytelling medium, demonstrable through a portfolio of design work and frontend code showcasing design systems, engaging microsites, Figma plugins, webGL experiments, CSS art, or anything else—you tell us&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and building public-facing websites that work elegantly across commonly used browsers and devices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A good understanding of the formal elements of design, not just limited to the web and including typography, layout, balance, and proportion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with React, with a focus on interactions, animation, performance, and polish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with A/B testing, synthetic monitoring, or accessibility testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Web Presence &amp;amp; Platform (WPP) is organized into two pillars: &lt;strong&gt;Platform&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Presence&lt;/strong&gt;. The Platform pillar builds internal systems, tooling, and infrastructure to support the web. The Presence pillar owns Stripe’s public-facing storytelling across &lt;strong&gt;stripe.com&lt;/strong&gt;, including our homepage, product landing pages, industry and solutions pages, and other high-impact go-to-market surfaces. Together, we shape how millions of people understand what Stripe is and what it can do for them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Designers on the Presence team work at the intersection of craft and impact—balancing clarity, polish, and systems thinking with strategic storytelling and experimentation. We collaborate closely with engineering, marketing, content, and product to deliver work that is not only beautiful, but measurably moves the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Designer on the Presence team, you&#39;ll contribute to the strategy and execution of Stripe’s most visible web surfaces. You’ll design new product pages, evolve storytelling for specific industries or audiences, and refine reusable patterns that make it easier to scale exceptional work across stripe.com. This is a high-impact role for a thoughtful, collaborative designer who deeply values visual craft, user clarity, and iteration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who’s excited to operate at the intersection of storytelling, systems, and scale—and who takes pride in the pixels. Your work will directly shape how millions of users understand Stripe, and help convert interest into action across a range of audiences—from founders to enterprise CTOs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design new and improved experiences across stripe.com, including product, industry, and solution landing pages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineers, PMMs, and content designers to define problems, explore solutions, and bring them to life&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with other designers to maintain and evolve systems that uphold Stripe’s design standards at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance storytelling with usability to create pages that are engaging, credible, and easy to navigate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use user research, user testing, and data to guide and validate your decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in critique and feedback sessions, contributing to the overall quality bar of the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate a meticulous attention to craft—ensuring designs are not only functional, but visually excellent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these, we encourage you to apply—even if you don’t meet every preferred qualification.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–4 years of relevant design experience, ideally in web or product marketing contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong portfolio of web design work that demonstrates exceptional &lt;strong&gt;visual design skills&lt;/strong&gt;, systems thinking, and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently scope and lead small to medium-sized projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and a collaborative mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in layout, typography, color, hierarchy, and interaction fundamentals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using Figma and working in component-based systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on CMS-driven websites and modular systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with front-end development workflows or an ability to speak fluently with engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of web performance, accessibility, and SEO best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing for international audiences or multilingual websites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in fast-paced, cross-functional environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care deeply about craft—but also about moving with urgency and focus. We seek feedback early and often, because we believe design gets stronger through collaboration and iteration. We keep our users front and center—whether that’s a small business owner evaluating Stripe for the first time, or a CTO trying to understand a complex product at a glance. And we take pride in delivering work that is not only beautiful and precise, but that delivers clear, measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value curiosity, humility, and resilience. You’ll do well here if you love to learn, enjoy working across disciplines, and bring energy and optimism into your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a great opportunity for someone eager to grow. Designers on the Presence team have gone on to lead major product launches, shape system-wide improvements, and take on leadership roles. You&#39;ll be supported by experienced peers and have space to develop your craft, influence, and ownership over time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Web Presence &amp;amp; Platform (WPP) is organized into two pillars—Platform and Presence. The Platform pillar builds internal systems, tooling, and infrastructure to support the web. The Presence pillar owns the public-facing storytelling across stripe.com and link.com—including our homepage, product landing pages, industry and solutions pages, and other high-impact go-to-market surfaces. Together, we shape how millions of people understand what Stripe is and what it can do for them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Designers on the Presence team work at the intersection of craft and impact—balancing clarity, polish, and systems thinking with strategic storytelling and experimentation. We collaborate closely with engineering, marketing, content, and product to deliver work that is not only beautiful, but measurably moves the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Designer on the Presence team, you&#39;ll own design across two distinct and high-visibility surface areas—Link (the Stripe one-click checkout experience and link.com) and Bridge (bridge.xyz—the Stripe stablecoin financial infrastructure, operating as its own standalone web property). These are some of the most strategically varied and creatively demanding surfaces in our portfolio—each with its own audience, brand voice, and design challenge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll operate with a high degree of autonomy—driving work from brief to launch, navigating ambiguity with confidence, and setting the quality bar for your focus areas. You&#39;ll shape the design systems and storytelling frameworks that make these surfaces scale, and you&#39;ll build deep expertise that makes you a go-to partner for the cross-functional teams you work alongside. This is a high-ownership role for a designer who is equally at home leading a complex project and sweating the details of a single layout.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end design of your focus areas, Link and Bridge, from early strategy through final delivery, with minimal oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive clarity in ambiguous or loosely defined briefs by synthesizing user needs, business goals, and technical constraints into a coherent point of view&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional collaboration with engineering, PMM, content design, brand, and product—facilitating alignment, integrating feedback, and keeping projects moving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with engineering throughout the design process, from exploring technical possibilities and constraints early, to co-creating solutions at the intersection of craft and code, and ensuring design intent carries through to final implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and advance design systems, patterns, and components specific to your surfaces, ensuring they are extensible and maintainable at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply and evolve visual and interaction standards that uphold the quality bar across diverse surface types—from immersive event experiences to conversion-focused product pages • Use research insights, user testing, and performance data to ground your decisions and advocate for the user across partner conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively contribute to team quality, sharing your expertise, setting an example in critique, and helping raise the standard of work across the Presence team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–7 years of relevant design experience, ideally in web, product marketing, or brand contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong portfolio demonstrating exceptional visual craft, systems thinking, and the ability to lead complex, multi-faceted design work independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to own projects end-to-end and deep fluency in layout, typography, color, motion, and interaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort navigating ambiguity: you can generate a clear plan from a loose brief and bring partners along with you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills: you articulate your thinking clearly, manage expectations proactively, and reduce confusion rather than add to it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Figma, experience working within component-based design systems, and fluency with AI design tools and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing for CMS-driven websites with modular, scalable systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing event or campaign-driven marketing experiences (conferences, product launches, brand moments)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with designing for financial products or developer audiences, where clarity and trust are design requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with front-end development workflows—you can collaborate meaningfully with engineers on what&#39;s possible and what&#39;s right&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing for international audiences, multilingual surfaces, or accessibility requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning or contributing to design across multiple distinct web properties or brand identities simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of advancing shared design patterns, systems, or tooling—not just using them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How we work&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care deeply about craft—but also about moving with urgency and focus. We seek feedback early and often, because we believe design gets stronger through collaboration and iteration. We keep our users front and center—whether that&#39;s a developer evaluating Stripe for the first time, a shopper encountering Link at checkout, or a fintech founder learning about Bridge. And we take pride in shipping work that is not only beautiful and precise, but that delivers clear, measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value curiosity, directness, and resilience. You&#39;ll do well here if you thrive in ownership, bring strong intuition without losing sight of the data, and are energized by complex problems that require both strategic clarity and exceptional craft.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Design organization builds the product and brand experiences that millions of businesses and developers rely on. We’re a cross-functional, global organization of product designers, content designers, design researchers, design systems engineers, motion designers, and design program specialists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to make economic infrastructure simple and accessible. Design plays a central role by making complex flows understandable, crafting clear product language, and building consistent systems that scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Design Operations team leads Design’s business operations, runs cross-organizational programs, and builds the systems that help teams collaborate and produce high-quality work. Design Program Managers guide complex programs through the design lifecycle and apply design thinking to our operating model. They prototype and iterate on how our team works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Design Program Manager to partner with the Research team. This full-time role reports to the Head of Design Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and build programs for the Research organization. Develop and implement processes and resources that support impactful research and scale the use of user insights across Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve our operating model and processes, including automating tasks, improving workflows, and developing repeatable methodologies. Measure the impact of these changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare researchers to use agentic workflows, including designing, building, and overseeing autonomous, multi-agent workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build custom tools, agents, automations, and skills for Research workflows and responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and implement new tools with researchers and cross-functional partners to support new capabilities across Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with researchers and designers across disciplines, skills, backgrounds, and specialties. Identify patterns and scale successful tools and approaches for broader team use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Research leadership and the Design Operations team to balance competing priorities and make effective use of team resources. Identify potential obstacles and risks to key programs. Develop solutions, solve problems effectively, and use decision-making frameworks to support timely resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source and evaluate third-party vendors when needed. Work with Legal, Security, and Procurement to onboard and pay vendors, including managing statements of work, business terms, and budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand research work. You have direct experience in Design or can quickly learn the workflows, deliverables, tools, and pressures relevant to Stripe researchers. You recognize that understanding someone’s work is necessary before changing it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have hands-on experience building artificial intelligence (AI) agents, automations, and tools. You’ve built solutions that changed how work gets done, and you can build alongside the people you support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an effective coach and communicator. You adapt your approach to different audiences and help people adopt new ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You recognize patterns and think in systems. When you build something that works for one person, you look for ways to make it useful to others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re persistent and versatile, with skills that can apply across the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You prioritize action and speed. You can show someone a useful proof of concept on their own deliverable today, while continuing to build toward longer-term platform goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in design thinking, qualitative or quantitative research, user experience, or program management, including experience partnering with research teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated hands-on experience building AI-powered tools, agents, automations, or workflows that improved real work processes for designers, researchers, creative teams, or product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coaching, teaching, or enabling others, formally or informally, with evidence of changes in how people work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences and adapt your style to different learners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across multiple workstreams and relationships at the same time. You’ll support a Research team that works across Stripe’s product, marketing, support, and design teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product-builder mindset for solving the last-mile problem: turning standalone AI experiments into polished, production-ready products that are easy to find and use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with research and design tooling ecosystems, such as Qualtrics, Sprig, Figma, Dovetail, or design system management tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI development tools and platforms, such as Claude, Claude Code, Codex, custom agent frameworks, application programming interface (API) integrations, or workflow automation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with change management, organizational transformation, or large-scale enablement programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and scaling internal tools, templates, or playbooks adopted beyond your immediate team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Narrative &amp;amp; Editorial team brings together Content Marketing, Brand Marketing, Portfolio Product Marketing, Copywriting, Copy Editing, and Customer Marketing. We create coherent, distinctive stories about the businesses, technologies, and economic forces shaping the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a senior editorial leader to help bring original stories and insights from Stripe–based on our data, expertise, and customer conversations–to a broader audience via media partnerships and other brand marketing channels. This person will be an exceptional editor, writer, and creative partner with strong instincts about what earns attention: an argument worth making, an unexpected angle, an elegant execution, or a piece of work that people genuinely want to share.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role reporting to the leader of Stripe’s Narrative &amp;amp; Editorial team. The role will spend most of its time shaping major external media partnerships, with the remainder split between helping with original editorial work and advising partner teams on new ideas and their execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the editorial and creative direction for Stripe’s most important external media partnerships, including advertising content, research-led collaborations, and original editorial programs developed with respected publishers and creators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop work that feels native to the audience and editorial environment in which it appears—not generic brand messaging placed beside someone else’s work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn Stripe’s original data analyses, economic insights, customer stories, and more into content pieces that are clear, surprising, useful, and memorable–and that readers and listeners won’t want to skip over.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the full editorial process for partnership work: refining briefs, identifying the strongest ideas, directing creative development, and providing decisive feedback on drafts and final deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct and manage agencies, external creators, and editorial partners as needed, working within existing partnership structures and commercial agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write, edit, and materially improve high-stakes content across formats, including blog posts, newsletter segments, podcast scripts, ad copy, social posts, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate original concepts for creative programs, editorial franchises, and nontraditional formats that broaden how Stripe contributes to conversations about the internet economy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted thought partner to teams across Stripe, helping them clarify ideas, find the strongest expression of their work, and make better creative decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with colleagues in Brand Marketing, Brand Design, Content Marketing, Portfolio PMM, Copywriting, and Customer Marketing to make Stripe’s storytelling more coherent and distinctive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and uphold a clear quality bar for editorial and partnership work, making well-reasoned calls about what is ready to represent Stripe and what still needs improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone with exceptional editorial judgment and a demonstrated ability to make complicated ideas compelling. You may have developed that experience in a newsroom, independent publication, creative studio, agency, research institution, technology company, or another rigorous creative environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 8+ years of relevant experience in editorial, writing, creative development, journalism, publishing, media, brand strategy, or a closely related field. This may include experience writing consistently for a large online followership, even if not professionally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an exceptional portfolio of published or public-facing work that demonstrates strong writing and editing, original thinking, and an ability to make ideas resonate with an audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are, in the best sense, very online: an active reader of and contributor to the newsletters, social platforms, and niche communities where people debate new ideas about technology, economics, science, business, and culture. You can spot emerging arguments, voices, and formats early—and engage with them authentically, with intellectual honesty and your own point of view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an excellent editor. You can diagnose what is missing from a draft or idea, identify the most interesting argument, and give feedback that makes the work materially better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience developing original editorial work, sponsored media, advertising, creative partnerships, or other high-quality audience-facing programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand the difference between work that is merely on-message and work that is genuinely interesting, useful, or worth discussing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can translate complex subjects—including technology, business, economics, science, or policy—into work that is accessible without becoming simplistic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong creative instincts and a sophisticated design sensibility. You understand how language, ideas, visuals, format, and distribution work together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are deeply curious about the technology industry and the broader cultural and economic context in which it operates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable influencing senior stakeholders, external partners, writers, designers, marketers, and agencies without relying on formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can move fluidly between strategy and execution: developing the core idea, shaping the brief, improving the draft, and making the final call on quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have high standards, sound judgment, and enough pragmatism to help teams make excellent work within real constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EMEA Demand Generation is a team of marketers and channel specialists that drive strategies to engage prospects and customers and generate demand for our prioritised solutions. We partner closely with global and regional Campaigns, Product Marketing, Field Marketing, Sales Development, and Sales teams to bring full-funnel product and audience campaigns to life, optimise performance, and drive business impact. Our team works across all customer segments and product lifecycle journeys, and at each stage of the customer lifecycle journey.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Platforms is one of the largest and fastest growing segments in Stripe. This role sits at the intersection of global and regional field teams and has a significant impact across our GTM organisation. From striving to better understand our customers to assessing the health of our business, you will help define and lead Stripe&#39;s Platform and Marketplaces strategy. Additionally, you will realise this strategy by driving marketing activations, building creative new programs, and working with sales and product to ensure full-funnel alignment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a highly collaborative individual who thinks both strategically and tactically to get things done, is comfortable navigating complexity and can work with both sales and marketing stakeholders. It is a business critical role and a great opportunity to build and have an impact across our GTM organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a multi-channel, regional demand generation strategy and plan to acquire SaaS Platforms and Marketplaces across EMEA in collaboration with global marketers and regional experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with global and regional performance media experts to acquire and re-engage customers through a broad mix of paid media tactics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Land global campaigns in region in conjunction with audience PMMs and global campaign leads to acquire and nurture leads at scale through digital content, paid placement, digital events, targeted nurture programs, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop account-based marketing strategies for named account lists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a cross-GTM coalition including Global Marketing, Regional Sales, Sales Development, and Sales Operations to jointly grow pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key business and revenue metrics for Platforms and Marketplaces across the full funnel while investigating business health issues such as conversion and lead quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally to define regional requirements as Stripe refines our marketing capabilities, MarTech stack, and lead management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify innovative ways to reach and engage our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a thought leader representing EMEA as we grow across our campaigns and broader go-to-market at Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continually optimise for efficiency, scale for growth, and prioritize for focus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years years of relevant experience running marketing campaigns for enterprise sized companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of paid media tactics, digital marketing strategies, marketing automation, email marketing tactics, account based marketing, and lead management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with Sales teams, including joint planning and execution, driving disciplined lead follow-up, and earning trust as a strategic business partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of defining and executing end-to-end, multi-channel programmes with a wide range of cross-functional stakeholders that deliver against funnel metrics and KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills; able to convey complex topics with simplicity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb organization and project management skills and the capacity to manage multiple complex projects at once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical skills and the ability to craft actionable insights from complex data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to work cross functionally in a highly matrixed organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A startup mentality with a bias to action and the ability to flex in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B2B marketing experience owning a regional demand generation strategy across multiple countries, customer segments, and products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the payments, financial technology, or adjacent industries, or marketing FinTech solutions or to FinTech companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a highly dynamic, high-growth tech company or consulting firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our professional services team combines payments and financial expertise with experience integrating Stripe technology in thousands of projects. We help our customers create marketplaces, launch subscription businesses, expand globally, and more. This team provides critical implementation and post-launch services to help Stripe users maximize long-term value, quickly and confidently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Engagement Managers lead complex and multi-faceted project teams that accelerate implementations and drive meaningful growth and innovation on the Stripe platform. As an Engagement Manager at Stripe, you will lead enterprises to become long-term Stripe users and advocates of our products and solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Professional Services provides a rapid path to success and ongoing value for our users. Our Engagement Managers enable users and partners to integrate Stripe’s solutions rapidly while delivering immediate impact and measurable value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive innovation and adoption of deployment practices, provide product adoption insights and help users achieve the maximum value from their Stripe investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively manage the integration of Stripe’s products into the user’s application/technical architecture, test and change management strategies and transformation timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver program management expertise based on experience, continuous learning, and in-depth knowledge of Stripe’s products and implementation best practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on the continuous improvement and enablement of the Stripe Implementation Methodology and it’s associate tools, templates and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide well-established program governance to manage requirements in line with the agreed scope and business objectives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide proactive risk assessment, prevention and mitigation plans and the efficient identification, tracking, and resolution of issues and decisions using established tools and templates with internal and user stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively drive interlock between the user and Stripe’s Product and Engineering teams to ensure alignment with Stripe’s roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a smooth transition of the implemented Stripe capabilities into operation for the user, including knowledge transfer and the handover to Stripe Support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in a global community of practitioners to continually evolve and improve the way in which Stripe leads and supports our Users through high impact and complex implementations of Stripe’s payment infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of consulting experience partnering with enterprise level strategic users on technology solutions, with a track record of top performance or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex business requirements and craft tailored solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly learn and explain technical concepts to Stripe’s largest users in a way which they will understand. Some may be deeply technical, others may be more business focussed, so you’ll need to talk to users in a language they can understand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven program management skills and experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong critical thinking skills, including the ability to identify suboptimal processes and drive more efficient ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to recognize repeated user-facing issues and build scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to engage with and lead executive stakeholders and key decision makers on the user side to drive towards an agreed outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in working with or in complex enterprise organizational and decision making structures&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to work collaboratively with and influence Stripe’s product and engineering teams to advocate for our users and continuously shape the forward roadmap of Stripe’s applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth stage Internet/Enterprise Software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry certifications to ensure project success. Typical certifications include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certified ScrumMaster&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PMP or PRINCE2 Certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in the payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A familiarity with the integration and testing of APIs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our professional services team combines payments and financial expertise with experience integrating Stripe technology in thousands of projects. We help our customers create marketplaces, launch subscription businesses, expand globally, and more. This team provides critical implementation and post-launch services to help Stripe users maximize long-term value, quickly and confidently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Engagement Managers lead complex and multi-faceted project teams that accelerate implementations and drive meaningful growth and innovation on the Stripe platform. As an Engagement Manager at Stripe, you will lead enterprises to become long-term Stripe users and advocates of our products and solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Professional Services provides a rapid path to success and ongoing value for our users. Our Engagement Managers enable users and partners to integrate Stripe’s solutions rapidly while delivering immediate impact and measurable value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver program management expertise based on experience, continuous learning, and in-depth knowledge of Stripe’s products and implementation best practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive innovation and adoption of deployment practices, provide product adoption insights and help users achieve the maximum value from their Stripe investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on the continuous improvement and enablement of the Stripe Implementation Methodology and its associated tools, templates and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide well-established program governance to manage requirements in line with the agreed scope and business objectives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively manage the integration of Stripe’s products into the user’s application/technical architecture, test and change management strategies and transformation timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide proactive risk assessment, prevention and mitigation plans and the efficient identification, tracking, and resolution of issues and decisions using established tools and templates with internal and user stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively drive interlock between the user and Stripe’s Product and Engineering teams to ensure alignment with Stripe’s roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a smooth transition of the implemented Stripe capabilities into operation for the user, including knowledge transfer and the handover to Stripe Support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in a global community of practitioners to continually evolve and improve the way in which Stripe leads and supports our Users through high impact and complex implementations of Stripe’s payment infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of consulting experience partnering with enterprise level strategic users on technology solutions, with a track record of top performance or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex business requirements and craft tailored solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly learn and explain technical concepts to Stripe’s largest users in a way which they will understand. Some may be deeply technical, others may be more business focussed, so you’ll need to talk to users in a language they can understand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven program management skills and experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong critical thinking skills, including the ability to identify suboptimal processes and drive more efficient ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to recognize repeated user-facing issues and build scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to engage with and lead executive stakeholders and key decision makers on the user side to drive towards an agreed outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in working with or in complex enterprise organizational and decision making structures&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to work collaboratively with and influence Stripe’s product and engineering teams to advocate for our users and continuously shape the forward roadmap of Stripe’s applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth stage Internet/Enterprise Software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry certifications to ensure project success. Typical certifications include: PMP, ITIL, PSM1, PSPO1.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in the payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A familiarity with the integration and testing of APIs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in Mandarin Chinese and English is required for this role, as it involves working primarily with clients within the Greater China market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
