&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Revenue and Financial Automation (RFA) team at Stripe is building a modern, revenue-focused, financial management platform for fast growing, digital native companies. Hundreds of thousands of businesses of all sizes and types use Stripe Billing to collect revenue for recurring and one-time payments across a variety of different pricing models—from selling SaaS subscriptions, to orchestrating multi-stage contracts, providing recovery and retention tools to prevent customer churn,—and with the acquisition of Metronome, delivering Usage-Based Billing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within this group, our team’s mission is to make Stripe and Metronome feel like one product, so merchants can bill for subscriptions and usage in a single, seamless experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Matching:&lt;/strong&gt; exact team matching for one of the subteams within this org will begin during final stages.&lt;em&gt; Please note we may also consider you for different orgs based on your experience, location, etc. &lt;/em&gt;More information on our team matching process can be found &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zvJkO2c7GzukHG-_oqc5wbOLajpuh5FjbmZPcZPU1o0/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.ahb3b6nrktv1&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for Full Stack engineers who are interested in building software services and platforms that impact thousands of employees and millions of Stripe users, regardless of whether they’re an end user, developer, or partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope, architect, and lead technical projects to improve on existing features and solve new problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain user-facing experiences, services, APIs, and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make effective tradeoffs that consider business priorities, user experience, and a sustainable technical foundation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute against both short- and long-term roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineers and product managers on infrastructure and other product teams to ensure your features are part of an integrated Stripe suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and uphold best practices in engineering, security, and technical design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-5+ years of industry software engineering experience (does not include internships nor includes co-ops)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding skills in any programming language &lt;em&gt;(we understand new languages can be learned on the job so our interview process is language agnostic)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills, can work across workstreams within your team and contribute to your peers’ success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the ability to thrive on a high level of autonomy, responsibility, and think of yourself as entrepreneurial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in working as a generalist across varying technologies and stacks to solve problems and delight both internal and external users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong AI adoption skills, proactively experiments with AI tools, adapts inefficient manual habits, and actively innovates to enhance performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of software development experience, with an emphasis on modern frontend technologies (HTML/CSS/TypeScript/React) and building delightful user interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies — from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups — use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support Experience Engineering builds the technology that powers Stripe&#39;s global support operations. Our engineers create the systems and services that support agents worldwide rely on every day to resolve issues for Stripe&#39;s millions of merchants and users — at scale, in real time, and across a growing range of channels and offerings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Case Resolution Platform team owns the core infrastructure and tooling that enables support agents around the world to do their best work. This includes case routing, live channels infrastructure spanning voice and messaging, machine translation, and integrations that connect Stripe&#39;s support stack to the platforms agents depend on.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for full-stack engineers who want to make an impact on the tools and infrastructure that power global customer support at scale. Our team collaborates with many cross-functional teams — from Infrastructure to Product to Operations — to deliver reliable, high-quality systems that support agents and merchants depend on every day. The team is actively expanding its live channels infrastructure to support new messaging platforms, including in Greater China, requiring collaboration with third-party providers in the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain full-stack services and infrastructure — spanning both backend systems and user-facing tooling — that support agents around the world rely on to resolve merchant and user issues in real time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand and deepen live channel integrations — including voice, messaging, and emerging platforms — across Stripe&#39;s global support operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug and solve critical production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal stakeholders across the company to build new features at large scale, while improving internal engineering standards, tooling, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively in a distributed and hybrid team, maintaining open communication and strong connections with colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of industry software engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native Mandarin fluency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-stack engineering experience, with front-end proficiency; React and Ruby are our primary technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb communication skills working with both technical and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reasoned judgement to unblock yourself and make rapid forward progress in ambiguous domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working as a generalist across varying technologies and stacks to solve problems and delight both internal and external users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User empathy and a customer-centric approach to problem solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or integrating third-party platform APIs, particularly in the communications or customer support tooling space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with real-time communication systems or messaging infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated technical leadership on ambiguous, impactful projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding and practical knowledge of cloud-based services (e.g., gRPC, GraphQL, Docker/Kubernetes, AWS, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Web Presence and Platform (WPP) is organized into two pillars, each of which is grouped into pods that focus on the central tenets of Stripe&#39;s public mission. The Presence pillar creates industry-leading designs for Stripe&#39;s front door surfaces, educates customers about the power of our platform, and drives our business success. The Platform pillar builds the internal machinery that powers these surfaces, and is responsible for making our websites fast, stable, and easy to modify.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP offers exciting opportunities to have a major impact on Stripe&#39;s success, as stripe.com is often a user&#39;s first impression of the company, and the vast majority of signups come via the website. We&#39;ll apply data-driven rigor to our curiosity, and we&#39;ll come up with clever ways to get insight into important questions. We&#39;ll have the leeway to test out-of-the-box ideas alongside incremental ones. We&#39;ll apply Stripe&#39;s users-first mentality both internally and externally, crafting tangible productivity and quality-of-life improvements for colleagues while maintaining and elevating the quality of stripe.com.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a software engineer, you&#39;ll design and build platforms and services that are configurable and scalable around the globe. You&#39;ll partner with many functions at Stripe, with the opportunity to both work on infrastructure and platform systems and produce direct user-facing business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Organizations is one of Stripe&#39;s biggest bets. You&#39;ll join a team with an ambitious and exciting goal at an early stage, with several opportunities to solve complex engineering problems at scale. If this sounds exciting, we&#39;d love to speak with you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain scalable, reliable, and performant services and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with a wide range of systems, processes, and technologies to own and solve technical and product problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and launch new capabilities and products that bring significant value to customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold our high engineering standards and elevate quality and engineering efficiency within our many codebases and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with stakeholders across the organization including dependency engineering teams, product, design, infrastructure, and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug production issues across services at multiple levels of the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background, including 3+ years of experience as a backend engineer, with an affinity for building scalable backend infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering, extending, and maintaining large-scale distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathetic, collaborative, and user-first mindset in everything you build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in working as a generalist across varying technologies and stacks to solve problems and delight both internal and external users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stitch together many different services even if you haven&#39;t worked with them before&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preference for simple solutions and designs over complex ones and good intuition for what is lasting and scalable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The skills to build holistically—from specs and documentation to implementation, testing, deployment, and measuring impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work well cross-functionally and earn trust from colleagues at all levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring and growing junior engineers as their technical leader&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fellow engineers feel they are able to learn from you, and you care deeply about mentoring others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propensity to ask questions, assume good intentions, and default to transparency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are often cited as the inspiration for engineers who join your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve worked to build pricing tooling that scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Payments Experiences group is an organization focused on bringing new and novel payment methods to Stripe, and ensuring Stripe&#39;s systems work well for merchants globally. This team works with internal and external partners to expand regional, non-card payment options, and to expand the use of Stripe&#39;s payments processing globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a São Paulo-based team, with platform teams in the US and Europe and sister teams worldwide. This team in particular will build and maintain new payment methods for Stripe, with a focus on LATAM and North America. They will manage local market idiosyncrasies, become regional experts that other Stripe teams will rely on, and partner with many non-tech functions at Stripe to expand our global reach and product portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and reason about integration experiences with a strong focus on end-user simplicity and developer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build back-end services and integrations across Stripe&#39;s payments product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage and interact with external partners to determine and build technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with users to understand their business needs and translate requirements into concrete solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams including product, partnerships, eng platforms, and other engineering teams to deliver these solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to software platforms used across payments at Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of full stack engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of verbal and written English language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building extensible, leveraged software solutions that scale to different kinds of user needs, with the ability to empathize with users and advocate for exceptional user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience working in payments and on payments technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience using Stripe products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Partnerships team develops and manages the strategic relationships that enable Stripe’s payments, financial-services, and geographic-expansion ambitions. We work with local payment methods, financial institutions, card networks, banks, and other ecosystem partners to build the infrastructure, commercial models, and market access Stripe needs to serve users globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a &lt;strong&gt;Global Partnerships Lead&lt;/strong&gt; based in Singapore to own Stripe’s Global Partnerships strategy and execution across Greater China, Hong Kong, and Singapore.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the regional Global Partnerships Lead, you will own Stripe’s most important in-market relationships across local payment methods, financial partners, card networks, banks, and expansion partners. You will set the partnership strategy for the region; identify, prioritize, and develop new opportunities; lead complex negotiations; and ensure partnerships deliver durable commercial, product, and expansion outcomes for Stripe and our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a leadership role at the intersection of product strategy, market expansion, and commercial execution. You will serve as Stripe’s senior partnership representative for the region, build trusted executive relationships with ecosystem partners, and lead alignment across Product, Engineering, Go-to-Market, Legal, Risk, Compliance, Finance, Treasury, and Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as Stripe’s &lt;strong&gt;Global Partnerships Lead for Greater China, Hong Kong, and Singapore&lt;/strong&gt;, with end-to-end accountability for the regional partnership portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute the regional strategy across local payment methods, financial partners, card networks, banks, and expansion partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Stripe’s senior external relationships in the region, building alignment and representing Stripe’s strategic priorities with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own partnership opportunities from market assessment and strategy through negotiation, contracting, onboarding, launch, governance, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regional expansion-partnership strategy and execution, coordinating the partnerships required to establish, operate, and scale Stripe in-market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate market intelligence, partner priorities, and ecosystem developments into clear recommendations for Stripe’s product and business strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional decision-making on commercial, product, operational, regulatory, and technical dependencies related to regional partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and manage partner-performance metrics, including commercial outcomes, product adoption, operational health, and strategic progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate and manage partnership risks, escalations, and trade-offs, ensuring sustained executive alignment internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a commercially rigorous, strategically minded partnerships leader who is deeply familiar with the payments ecosystem in Greater China, Hong Kong, and Singapore. You are comfortable navigating complex stakeholder environments, structuring ambiguous opportunities, and independently driving high-impact outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, corporate development, strategy, financial services, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in payments, fintech, ecommerce, banking, card networks, local payment methods, or adjacent financial-services sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading complex, strategic commercial negotiations with senior external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the payments and financial-partnership landscape in Greater China, Hong Kong, and/or Singapore, including relevant market dynamics and business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and English executive communication skills and business-level Mandarin proficiency, written and spoken as this role would require working closely with our users and partners in the Greater China region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to develop a clear point of view amid ambiguity, influence without authority, and drive decisions across complex internal and external stakeholder groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with product and engineering organizations on partnerships with meaningful technical, operational, and regulatory dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate autonomously while balancing multiple high-priority initiatives and long-term strategic relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a regional or multi-market portfolio of payments or financial-infrastructure partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting market-entry, expansion, licensing, or ecosystem-development initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing senior relationships across banks, networks, payment-method providers, fintechs, or other relevant ecosystem partners in the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a fast-paced, global technology company with cross-functional product, commercial, and regulatory stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team and the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The People Systems Operations Administrator supports the day-to-day work that keeps Stripe’s People technology running accurately and reliably. The role sits in the Service Delivery Center and works as part of the wider People Solutions team, with a close dotted-line partnership to People Solutions Systems Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own a defined set of routine tier 1 and tier 2 operational work across Workday and related People Systems. This includes monitoring support channels and system inboxes, triaging requests, completing repeatable administrative tasks, maintaining documentation, and routing complex issues to the right People Systems owner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on operations role. It creates clearer separation between routine support work and the configuration, architecture, governance, and project delivery owned by the People Systems team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support queue and request triage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Monitor the Salesforce case management queue and Jira requests for People Systems work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage incoming requests by urgency, business impact, data sensitivity, and defined support process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve standard requests using documented procedures, and route exceptions or higher-complexity work to the appropriate People Systems owner.&lt;br&gt;Keep request records accurate and complete, including status updates, required approvals, supporting documentation, and clear handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring request patterns and flag opportunities to improve documentation, self-service, or system processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workday operations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the Workday inbox for business process errors, stuck transactions, alerts, and other operational issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete routine Workday support tasks, including standard access requests, account maintenance, and operational follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Salesforce and JIRA run work and respond to common People Systems questions using approved guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help with recurring operational tasks such as account monitoring, account resets, and quarterly account reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support year-end activity, including schedule extensions, alert configuration, audit requests, and tracking follow-up items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with release readiness by reviewing assigned Workday updates, completing test steps, documenting results, and escalating issues found during testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support recurring People programs, such as performance-cycle launches, using established runbooks and checklists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting, documentation, and Jira support &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intake and triage Workday reporting and data requests. Confirm required information, route requests to the right owner, and provide status updates to requesters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete standard reporting tasks and access-related requests where there is a documented process and appropriate approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain runbooks, Trailhead content, standard operating procedures, and request templates so guidance stays current and easy to find.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support data-quality checks and follow established processes to correct or escalate issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnership with People Systems &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with People Systems analysts and engineers to understand support priorities, upcoming releases, recurring work, and escalation paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear handoffs for work that requires configuration changes, advanced reporting, integrations, security decisions, or policy interpretation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in regular reviews of queue trends, service levels, documentation gaps, and operational risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build platform knowledge over time, with opportunities to take on more complex administration and configuration work as skills develop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in People operations, HR administration, systems support, service delivery, or another operations role involving high-volume, process-driven work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail, particularly where accuracy affects People records, access, payroll, compliance, or reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work through a queue independently, prioritize requests, follow defined processes, and escalate issues at the right time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication and comfort giving requesters concise status updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Jira, Salesforce, or a similar case-management or ticketing tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort learning enterprise systems and following structured procedures across multiple tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organization skills and a consistent approach to documenting work and following requests through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good judgment when working with confidential information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Workday, including Core HCM, business processes, security administration, reporting, or Workday inbox monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling reporting requests, data access requests, and standard user provisioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting cyclical People programs, compliance activities, audit requests, or system-release testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within the first six months, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the defined tier 1 and routine tier 2 People Systems queue work with accurate, timely resolution and clear escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish dependable monitoring for People Systems tickets in Salesforce, JIRA, the Workday inbox, and recurring operational tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce avoidable handoffs and ensure complex work reaches the right People Systems owner with the context needed to act.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep core runbooks and self-service guidance current based on recurring request patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give People Systems analysts and engineers more capacity for configuration, governance, architecture, and strategic delivery work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who are we?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;About Stripe&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Delivery Center (SDC) strategy will provide operational leverage and expand Stripe’s portfolio of operational capabilities to support the scaled needs for external users and internal Stripe teams. Stripe’s People &amp;amp; Places Operations team will sit within the SDC and is a highly collaborative, cross-functional team that drives key support for the People and Places function. We work with many different teams at Stripe. We are nimble and flexible individuals that can wear many different hats. We don’t mind working through ambiguity and love adding organization to chaos. We believe that success is not defined by any one individual, but rather by the collective work of the entire team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Provide strategic HR leadership to HR Operations. Effectively manage, develop and engage the global team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure an exceptional employee experience by simplifying key processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and implement HR initiatives and projects which are aligned within HR and Centers of Expertise (COE)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and lead key projects for improvement across HR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify best practices that can be applied to improve work tasks and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver service improvement activity across HR through employing process improvement methodologies and the application of innovative thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote and lead change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports the administration and maintenance of HR systems while driving process and data integrity across the HR landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in and/or lead projects aimed at expanding centralization, leverage technology to improve the employee experience, and discover actionable insights and recommend solutions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for driving process consistency, data integrity and compliance to HR policies, procedures, data privacy, audit controls and regulatory requirements in all HR Service Center activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serves as the escalation point for HR Operations guiding the root cause analysis, resolution and communication protocol&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the case management system (Ops ticketing system) and team to establish service level agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the HRIS team supporting HR technology upgrades&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain team standard operating procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversees relevant employee data management to ensure that data is secure and maintained consistent with company policies and privacy regulations and that required reporting and filings are delivered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track HR metrics to identify areas for improvement. Develop and implement counter-measures to correct identified misses to goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in verbal &amp;amp; written communication in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good working knowledge of MS Office, MS Outlook; MS Excel. Proficiency is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze and identify patterns in large data sets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decision making aptitudes based on given guidelines and in ambiguous contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be comfortable working with large data sets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very good knowledge and experience in internet navigation and research – finding specific information about products in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 7+ years of people and operations management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education - Grad/Post Grad in human resources or a related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desired 12+ years of overall experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with HR systems such as Workday, Greenhouse, Confluence and Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously with minimal supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership skills, data analytical &amp;amp; presentation skills, Written &amp;amp; Communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of overall HR lifecycle – &lt;strong&gt;Core HR&lt;/strong&gt;, Benefits, Talent Mobility, Equity, Compensation, Exits etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Growth Marketing is a team of performance-driven marketers and channel specialists. We partner closely with growth, creative, analytics and regional marketing to drive revenue through self-serve and sales motions. We work globally, across all Stripe offerings and with all company segments — from startups to the largest enterprises.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a China Growth Marketer, you will own launching, proving out, and scaling paid media and growth marketing channels for the Chinese market. This is a 0-to-1 role: you&#39;ll identify the right channels, build the playbooks, and demonstrate what works before scaling investment. You&#39;ll work across paid channels native to China (WeChat, Baidu, Douyin, Xiaohongshu, Zhihu, Bilibili, and others), as well as broader growth marketing levers like web optimization, content distribution, and landing page localization for Chinese users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the in-house expert on how to reach Chinese developers, founders, and business operators through digital channels, bringing deep knowledge of the local ecosystem, platform mechanics, regulatory environment, and user behavior. You&#39;ll partner cross-functionally with regional marketing, analytics, creative, product marketing, and sales to ensure paid media supports Stripe&#39;s growth objectives in China.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch and scale paid media channels specific to the China market — including WeChat Ads, Baidu SEM, Douyin/Ocean Engine, Xiaohongshu, Zhihu, Bilibili, and programmatic platforms (e.g., Tencent Guangdiantong, ByteDance Pangolin)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a testing roadmap to prove channel viability: define hypotheses, run experiments, measure incrementality, and make go/no-go recommendations on scaling investment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own web optimization and landing page localization for Chinese audiences — ensuring Stripe&#39;s web presence converts effectively for local users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build measurement frameworks for China-specific channels, partnering with analytics to attribute performance through to signups, activations, and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage campaign budgets, pacing, and performance reporting — communicating results clearly to stakeholders across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring the skills and experience to unblock, set up and navigate media platforms and partnerships in the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on China&#39;s digital marketing landscape: platform algorithm changes, content regulations, privacy laws (PIPL), and emerging channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional marketing, sales, and product marketing to align paid media with broader China go-to-market strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write concise performance updates and strategic recommendations for a global audience that ranges from paid media specialists to senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of digital marketing experience with significant hands-on experience running paid campaigns on China-native platforms (WeChat, Baidu, Douyin, Xiaohongshu, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High professional fluency in Mandarin Chinese and English — able to write ad copy, review creative, and communicate strategy in both languages as this role will be heavily involved in the businesses in the Greater China region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the China digital marketing ecosystem: platform mechanics, ad formats, targeting capabilities, content regulations, and user behavior patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching new channels from scratch — demonstrated ability to take a channel from 0 to 1, prove its value, and scale it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills — ability to analyze campaign data, identify trends, and make data-driven optimization decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in B2B marketing, SaaS, developer tools, fintech, or high-growth technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter mentality — ability to drive strategic and tactical work forward with minimal oversight in a fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication skills — can write concise, clear updates for a global audience with varying levels of paid media expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of digital marketing experience with deep China market specialization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing to developers or technical audiences in China&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with China-specific analytics and attribution tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with web optimization, CRO, or landing page testing for Chinese audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of China&#39;s regulatory environment as it relates to digital advertising (PIPL, CAC content regulations, industry-specific ad restrictions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a global company with cross-timezone collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Go-to-Market (GTM) Planning Strategy and Operations team works at the intersection of corporate planning, GTM Strategy, Product, GTM and Regional Strategy and Operations with responsibility for ensuring that we land the Stripe annual rhythm in a smooth and timely manner. This entails three main pillars:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Building and landing foundations (tooling, process, and strategic changes) for next cycle • Ensuring budgets, territories, targets, comp plans, reporting, and enablement are delivered to GTM in a timely manner • Effectively managing in-year Account, Territory, Quota, and Adjustments&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within this organization, the Central Policy and Operations team owns the processes, systems, and automation that power territory management, account placement, segmentation, and business adjustments at scale—processing over 10,000 account movements per month and operating critical workflows that serve the entire GTM organization at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking an experienced systems practitioner to own the end-to-end processes, Mechanization and Automation pillar for Central Operations end-to-end. In this role, you&#39;ll be the person who wakes up every day focused on ensuring our support tooling has a clear roadmap, our processes are documented and AI-enabled, and our operational systems are built to scale without adding headcount.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll take ownership of how we design, build, and evolve the systems that underpin Stripe&#39;s territory, segmentation, quota, and adjustment infrastructure. This means moving beyond maintaining what exists today—you&#39;ll architect what comes next. You&#39;ll drive the transition from legacy tooling toward Stripe-native solutions, reduce contractor dependency through intelligent automation, and ensure every process is auditable, documented, and delegatable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who understands the difference between automating a broken process and redesigning it before automation—and has the experience to know which one to do when. Additionally, being able to work cross-functionally at 500-foot collaboration and working at 20,000 feet as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Own the process and tooling roadmap for Central Policy and Operations independently, setting short-to-medium-term strategic direction and aligning investment to areas of greatest need &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Drive cross-functional initiatives across GTM, Finance Systems, and Data Engineering to align territory, quota, and adjustment data for AI enablement &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Architect the path to transition off external tools toward Stripe-native tooling—building the business case, influencing resource allocation, and measuring ROI &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Design and implement automation for Account Team assignments, User Segmentation updates, and Manager and Approval workflows in Salesforce to reduce manual intervention and contractor dependency &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Build audit frameworks, compliance metrics, and governance processes for scaled systems (Territory Assignments, Quota, Workflows, Adjustment Approvals)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Establish documentation, process architecture, and AI-ready task design that enables leadership visibility, vendor onboarding, and repeatable delegation &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Anticipate system integration risks and resolve them before they become escalations—including cross-system data movement between Salesforce, territory engines, and reporting infrastructure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 or more years of experience in business operations, systems development, technical program management, or a related discipline with demonstrated progression in scope and complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of owning and delivering end-to-end systems or tooling programs in a cross-functional environment—from business case through implementation and ongoing optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL proficiency and experience with data architecture, pipeline design, or systems integration work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading process redesign and automation initiatives that delivered measurable operational efficiency or cost reduction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence senior stakeholders, build investment cases, and drive decisions across functions without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communicator who can translate complex technical concepts for non-technical audiences and leadership, and translate business requirements into system specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience with Anaplan, Salesforce, Approval Workflows, or Process design and administration, configuration, or development (flows, automation, data management) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with territory management, sales operations planning cycles, or GTM systems at scale &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Background in designing processes for AI enablement—structured documentation, task decomposition, and governance frameworks &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience managing vendor relationships or coordinating with external implementation partners&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The GTM Product Marketing team sits within Stripe&#39;s Product Marketing org. We make sure Stripe sellers walk into every conversation prepared, confident, and armed with the right story. As Stripe&#39;s center of excellence for general product enablement, we set the standard for how sellers learn and pitch our products, drive consistency across product suites, and act as Marketing&#39;s Voice of the Field — surfacing seller insights to sharpen upstream messaging and positioning. We translate product value into seller-ready narratives, resources, and enablement — and we measure our impact on seller confidence and how effectively our teams pitch, qualify, and close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Commerce Experiences products (Optimized Checkout Suite, Link, Terminal, Agentic Commerce) help businesses convert more customers across every channel — from online checkout, to digital wallets, to in-person commerce, to the emerging world of AI-driven shopping. We&#39;re looking for an exceptional GTM product marketer to bring Stripe&#39;s story to market. In this role, you&#39;ll be the connective tissue between product, marketing, and the field. You&#39;ll translate complex commerce and checkout capabilities into compelling narratives and seller resources that resonate with our users and drive adoption. You&#39;ll equip customer-facing teams to confidently pitch all our solutions, answer technical questions, and speak to the roadmap. You&#39;ll also elevate seller and field insights to refine product positioning and messaging.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the GTM PMM for Commerce Experiences, you’ll need to quickly build a deep understanding of Stripe’s Commerce Experiences products, buyer personas, and differentiation. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the content development and GTM enablement strategy across the sold funnel — creating seller-ready resources (pitch decks, FAQs, value props, talking points) that translate product positioning into clear, differentiated customer value propositions for enterprise, mid-market, and platform buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Market Intelligence to monitor and understand commerce, checkout, and emerging agentic commerce market trends, competitive dynamics, and seller-facing competitive narratives — synthesize insights, and leverage these to build differentiated positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver training programs that build seller expertise across the Commerce Experiences portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare sellers for major product launch events like Stripe Sessions, and to understand the details of the roadmap product is building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage data and insights to identify enablement and knowledge gaps, prioritize asset development, launch new content, and measure effectiveness on seller confidence and other KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface field insights on a regular cadence — through monthly readouts and structured retros — to inform core PMM positioning and product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of product marketing experience, preferably in B2B tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with checkout, ecommerce, digital wallets, agentic commerce or other commerce platforms is strongly preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Enterprise sales cycles and technical products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation abilities, with a proven track record of distilling complex strategies into clear, compelling narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to move quickly without compromising attention to detail or polish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who thrives in fast-paced, ambiguous environments and can manage multiple priorities simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with data-driven decision making and measuring marketing impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively with stakeholders across Product, Sales, and Marketing, and contribute to alignment on shared goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated comfort working with, and presenting to, senior leaders across a variety of disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills, a tendency to seek and share alternative views, and an ability to earn stakeholder confidence&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using or building AI-powered tooling to accelerate seller productivity or content development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recruiting team seeks to build the culture of Stripe by aligning the strongest global talent to our highest impact business needs. They focus on bringing Stripe’s operating principles to life in their recruiting processes, providing the highest-quality candidate experience, and leveraging data driven storytelling to influence the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To further this important mission, we are looking for consultative and creative recruiters to grow and scale our Go-to-Market (GTM) team. The GTM organization at Stripe encompasses our Sales team, Marketing and Sales Development, GTM and Product Operations, and Professional Services. These teams are expanding in the region, focusing on bringing new users onto the Stripe platform, supporting our existing users&#39; scale, and growing their businesses. You can expect high impact and wide-ranging responsibilities: owning full-cycle recruiting, driving hiring strategy, and delivering best-in-class candidate experience. This person must be a builder who thrives in a learning environment—unafraid to try new things, embrace new ideas, and welcome suggestions for how we can iterate on our processes. This is an 11 month fixed-term contract.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders across the organization to understand their hiring objectives and develop recruiting strategies aimed at achieving headcount goals, with an emphasis on expanding our GTM teams in EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose and implement creative and scalable changes to the existing recruiting strategy to enhance efficacy and reach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze recruiting metrics, providing regular reports on hiring progress to business leadership to ensure transparency and alignment with goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategic sourcing plans to identify and engage top talent, ensuring a robust and inclusive candidate pool for current and future hiring needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular market research and analysis to stay informed about talent trends in the EMEA region, using insights to inform recruiting strategies and address potential challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with cross-functional teams—including Finance, People Ops, Benefits, Onboarding, and Legal—to deliver a seamless and high-quality candidate experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of full-cycle Recruiting experience in a fast-paced, high-growth environment including in house experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including business proficiency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to build relationships with senior leaders and effectively influence decision-making processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong drive to identify and engage top talent, fostering relationships with candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to utilize data insights to identify trends and refine recruiting processes, enhancing efficiency and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility, adept at shifting tasks and priorities in response to changing circumstances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recruiting team seeks to build the culture of Stripe by aligning the strongest global talent to our highest impact business needs. They focus on bringing Stripe’s operating principles to life in their recruiting processes, providing the highest-quality candidate experience, and leveraging data driven storytelling to influence the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To further this important mission, we are looking for consultative and creative recruiters to grow and scale our Go-to-Market (GTM) team. The GTM organization at Stripe encompasses our Sales team, Marketing and Sales Development, GTM and Product Operations, and Professional Services. These teams are expanding in the region, focusing on bringing new users onto the Stripe platform, supporting our existing users&#39; scale, and growing their businesses. You can expect high impact and wide-ranging responsibilities: owning full-cycle recruiting, driving hiring strategy, and delivering best-in-class candidate experience. This person must be a builder who thrives in a learning environment—unafraid to try new things, embrace new ideas, and welcome suggestions for how we can iterate on our processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategic sourcing plans to identify and engage top talent, ensuring a robust and inclusive candidate pool for current and future hiring needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular market research and analysis to stay informed about talent trends, using insights to inform recruiting strategies and address potential challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders across the organization to understand their hiring objectives and develop recruiting strategies aimed at achieving headcount goals, with an emphasis on expanding our GTM teams across the US, LatAM and Canada&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze recruiting metrics, providing regular reports on hiring progress to business leadership to ensure transparency and alignment with goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose and implement creative and scalable changes to the existing recruiting strategy to enhance efficacy and reach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with cross-functional teams—including Finance, People Ops, Benefits, Onboarding, and Legal—to deliver a seamless and high-quality candidate experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of full-cycle Recruiting experience in a fast-paced, high-growth environment including in house experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to build relationships with senior leaders and effectively influence decision-making processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong drive to identify and engage top talent, fostering relationships with candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to utilize data insights to identify trends and refine recruiting processes, enhancing efficiency and outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility, adept at shifting tasks and priorities in response to changing circumstances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS), such as Greenhouse, Lever, or similar platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging sourcing and CRM tools (e.g., Gem, LinkedIn Recruiter) to build and manage talent pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of recruiting analytics and reporting tools to drive data-informed hiring strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with scheduling, communication, and collaboration tools (e.g., GoodTime, Slack, G Suite)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly adopt new recruiting technologies and optimize workflows for scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and create new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the gross domestic product of the internet, and we have a significant amount of work ahead. That means you have an opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing some of the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Recruiting team’s mission is to build Stripe’s teams by identifying and attracting people who can help us increase the gross domestic product of the internet. We work closely with business leaders to understand their goals, anticipate talent needs, and develop thoughtful hiring strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Go-to-Market (GTM) Sourcer supporting the Americas, you’ll help grow teams across Sales. You’ll partner with recruiters and hiring leaders to understand each role, map relevant talent markets, engage prospective candidates, and build strong pipelines across the United States, Latin America, and Canada.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a strategic, data-oriented Sourcer who can find and engage exceptional GTM talent in competitive and evolving markets. You’ll own the top-of-funnel strategy for a portfolio of roles, translating business needs into targeted sourcing plans and strong candidate pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll combine market research, creative outreach, recruiting technology, and internal networks to reach prospective candidates. You’ll also provide recruiters and hiring leaders with clear insights into talent availability, pipeline health, and the changes needed to meet hiring goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with recruiters and hiring leaders to understand hiring goals, role requirements, and the profiles most likely to succeed at Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and run sourcing strategies for GTM roles across Sales and Solutions Architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, engage, and assess prospective candidates, then manage them through the initial stages of the recruiting process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build broad candidate pipelines using direct sourcing, referrals, internal networks, talent communities, events, and other relevant channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct talent research and market mapping to assess talent availability, identify target companies and adjacent profiles, and inform hiring plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use qualitative and quantitative data to evaluate pipeline health, outreach performance, conversion, and sourcing effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share clear market and pipeline insights with recruiters and hiring leaders, including risks, tradeoffs, and recommended changes to sourcing strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain long-term relationships with prospective candidates, including talent who may be a fit for future opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test new sourcing approaches, tools, and outreach methods, then turn successful practices into repeatable processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Talent Brand and other Recruiting teams on campaigns, events, and initiatives that expand awareness of Stripe’s opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver a thoughtful, responsive candidate experience that reflects Stripe’s values throughout the sourcing process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements below. If you meet these requirements, we encourage you to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 or more years of sourcing or recruiting experience in a fast-paced environment, with experience building pipelines for GTM roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using sourcing and candidate relationship management tools, such as Gem and LinkedIn Recruiter, to identify and engage prospective candidates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to create sourcing strategies for competitive, specialized, or difficult-to-fill roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to create personalized outreach and represent opportunities accurately and persuasively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build effective working relationships with recruiters, hiring managers, candidates, and senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong research and analytical skills, with experience using sourcing metrics and market information to identify trends and adjust strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize and manage multiple candidate pipelines across roles, locations, and stages of the hiring process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and a problem-solving mindset, including the ability to learn unfamiliar talent markets and develop creative approaches when established sourcing channels aren’t producing results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to adjust priorities and sourcing plans as business needs and market conditions change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience sourcing for GTM, specifically Sales and Solutions Architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with applicant tracking systems such as Greenhouse or Lever.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with recruiting analytics, reporting tools, and talent-market research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using events, talent communities, referrals, or brand campaigns to create new candidate pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of adopting new recruiting technologies and improving sourcing workflows at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

