&lt;p&gt;The Capabilities team sits within the Global Partnerships organization and is a key part of Stripe’s success. We develop and execute high-impact product partnership initiatives and strategies with card network partners, including Visa, Mastercard, and American Express.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work helps shape Stripe’s product strategy and deliver capabilities for Stripe users, including agentic commerce and stablecoin pilots.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Partner Development Manager on the Capabilities team, you will define and execute high-impact product partnership strategies with Stripe’s card network partners. You will use deep payments expertise to identify opportunities, shape joint strategies and commercial models, and lead cross-functional execution for new capabilities that support Stripe’s long-term priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with Product, Engineering, Legal, Finance, Risk, Compliance, Treasury, and senior external stakeholders. You will develop partner requirements, define deal strategy, lead complex negotiations, and drive alignment across multiple teams and partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute product partnership strategies and joint initiatives with Stripe’s most critical card network partners, including new offerings that benefit Stripe users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, evaluate, and make the case for high-impact partnership opportunities, using industry expertise, partner context, and cross-functional input.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop commercial models, partnership approaches, and distribution plans for new product capabilities and go-to-market motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently lead complex, high-impact negotiations with card network partners, including commercial agreements that affect Stripe’s payment acceptance costs and long-term strategic position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create scalable deal structures and partnership frameworks that can be applied across partners, products, or markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence internal product and go-to-market teams, as well as external partner stakeholders, to develop solutions that meet the needs of Stripe, its users, and the evolving payments landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional workstreams across Product, Engineering, Legal, Finance, Risk, Compliance, and Treasury. Set direction, clarify trade-offs, and align stakeholders on the resources and commitments needed to execute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve complex stakeholder friction with minimal direction, including competing product priorities, partner requirements, commercial considerations, and delivery timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess Stripe and partner readiness for major initiatives, surface risks and dependencies, and advocate for the decisions needed to move work forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure sound execution of day-to-day partnership operations and adherence to risk and compliance obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe at partner and industry events, and build trusted relationships with senior partner stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements for this role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in strategic partnerships, business development, corporate development, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in payments, card networks, or a related financial services domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on card issuing products, issuer-facing capabilities, or product partnerships involving issuing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough understanding of card network dynamics, business models, and the payments ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad and deep experience crafting and executing industry-wide partnership strategies, product strategies, or go-to-market models that deliver significant impact across multiple partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining and leading complex partnership strategies that require alignment across product, commercial, operational, and technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently leading complex, high-impact commercial negotiations and managing trade-offs across economics, product capabilities, timelines, and strategic objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in product-centric environments with significant internal and external dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to influence senior stakeholders internally and externally across a wide range of functions, including C-suite leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bridge is building financial infrastructure that makes money more programmable and global. The Financial Partnerships team develops the ecosystem that powers Bridge and Stripe’s stablecoin products and financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team works across Bridge and Stripe to develop strategic relationships with banks, exchanges, asset managers, liquidity providers, and stablecoin ecosystem partners. These partnerships support reserve management, liquidity, distribution, and card-related products for both businesses and their shared customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior Partnership Development Manager, you will define and execute the financial-partnership strategy that powers Bridge and Stripe’s stablecoin products and financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own a strategic ecosystem of financial-partner relationships across markets. You will turn market insight into durable, high-impact partnerships, from strategy and negotiation through launch, expansion, and ongoing performance management. You will work directly with senior Stripe leaders and external executives to make investment tradeoffs, align priorities, and shape long-term product and partnership strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and lead multi-year partnership strategy across reserves, liquidity, distribution, card-related products, and the stablecoin ecosystem, using market and commercial insight to shape Bridge and Stripe priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a strategic financial-partner ecosystem across markets, including partnership health, commercial performance, executive alignment, escalations, and expansion opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source, evaluate, structure, negotiate, and lead high-impact partnerships with banks, exchanges, asset managers, liquidity providers, and stablecoin ecosystem partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set end-to-end deal strategy for complex, novel, or multi-market partnerships with material financial, product, operational, or regulatory implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead company-level tradeoffs across partner economics, customer needs, product requirements, operational readiness, risk, and long-term strategic value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Treasury, Legal, Compliance, Risk, Operations, Finance, Engineering, and go-to-market teams to set requirements, align senior stakeholders, and execute shared priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a differentiated point of view on financial services and digital assets, represent Stripe and Bridge with senior external stakeholders, and share expertise that strengthens the broader Partnerships organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in strategic partnerships, business development, corporate development, strategic finance, treasury, or a related field, including ownership of complex, high-impact external partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently set partnership strategy, influence senior executives, and drive cross-functional alignment on ambiguous, high-stakes company priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of structuring, negotiating, and managing high-value, multi-year partnerships with material strategic, financial, product, operational, or regulatory implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience working with financial institutions or infrastructure providers, such as banks, exchanges, asset managers, market makers, liquidity providers, payments companies, or stablecoin ecosystem participants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial judgment and experience leading both commercial and technical partnership conversations with senior internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in stablecoins, crypto, card issuing, or stablecoin-linked card programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing partnership strategy across multiple markets or partner types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience representing a company with industry groups, at conferences, or with senior external executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring or guiding peers on partnership strategy, complex negotiations, or cross-functional execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Payment Methods and Expansion Partnerships team develops and manages relationships with payment methods and financial partners that enable Stripe’s product strategy, and delivers new capabilities in new and existing markets to Stripe users.&amp;nbsp; This is not a traditional sales, channel, merchant-partnership, or account-management role. You will build product and infrastructure partnerships with banks, acquirers, payment providers, and other financial institutions that enable Stripe’s products and market launches. Our team executes on high-impact, cross-functional initiatives across new products, geographic expansion, user advocacy, and policy. These partnerships have a significant impact on Stripe and the products used by millions of our users.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a new member to join our team to develop and execute on high-impact initiatives with both payment method partners and expansion partners in new and existing markets, focussing on EMEA. These partnerships form the basis of Stripe’s product. As part of these efforts, you will be responsible for deal negotiation and execution for our EMEA payment methods and expansion business. This is an exciting opportunity to make a significant impact and contribute to the growth and success of Stripe&#39;s payment method partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will require close coordination with product and engineering teams, as well as cross-functional stakeholders including go to market teams, Marketing, Legal, Finance, Risk, etc., and with external partners’ senior executives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities and craft partnership and product strategies for market expansion and payment method partners in existing markets in EMEA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute deals, manage partner onboarding and partnership development for new and existing financial partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand our partners’ strategic priorities, challenges, and internal roadmaps; regularly communicate insights and recommendations to Stripe product stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and grow Stripe’s relationships with partners, identifying&amp;nbsp; partner stakeholders who will champion Stripe, and building alignment between Stripe and our partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish key performance indicators (KPIs) and metrics to measure the effectiveness of both deal&amp;nbsp; processes and ongoing partner management and&amp;nbsp; distribution initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, corporate development or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience related to payments and/or ecommerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep EMEA market knowledge, and a thorough understanding of payment method dynamics and business models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong agency, can handle ambiguity in a fast-moving organization, and thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple stakeholders with varying priorities and drive creative solutions and commitment to a shared goal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a product centric environments with significant internal and external dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills with the ability to influence stakeholders internally and externally across a wide variety of functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Alliances and Channels team focuses on building, supporting, and going to market with professional services firms including systems integrators, consultancies, and managed services providers such as Accenture, PwC, Deloitte, Infosys, and others. In addition, the team leads the go-to-market initiatives with our strategic technology alliance partners including AWS, Salesforce, Adobe, and others. Our objective is to ensure users have access to the broadest set of solutions leveraging the Stripe platform and the deepest set of technology and industry experts, while at the same time ensuring our partners and Stripe build large, mutually beneficial businesses together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategic Global Alliances team focuses on a subset of our highest priority partnerships. These partnerships operate at global scale with Stripe and present opportunities to create significant sales pipeline, deals sold, joint solutions, and scaled delivery expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll support the overall success of Stripe&#39;s Global Alliance with Accenture and other key GSIs in EMEA, driving joint GTM and co-sell. You&#39;ll work alongside the Accenture Global Partner Development Manager and other GSI PDMs to drive net new demand for the partnership in the field across key markets in EMEA. This position is focused on deepening our joint sales motion, joint solutions, and delivery capabilities. This position is fast-paced, highly visible, and aligned to quarterly metrics. As a Partner Development Manager, you&#39;ll hold a holistic view of the business, generated by and engaged with Accenture and other partners in EMEA, and work across the Stripe Sales segments to enhance and grow partner-related Stripe revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work cross-functionally with Partner Sales Managers, Partner Development Leadership, and Stripe AEs. You&#39;ll demonstrate an understanding of the Stripe Partner Ecosystem and the Stripe sales organization, and recognize high-impact opportunities, solutions, support deals for successful engagement with partners, and maintain high business hygiene.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll drive towards end-customer value that results in business growth to both Accenture (and other GSIs) and Stripe by being partner-centric in all activities, serving as a leader and advocate for them within Stripe, and accurately representing Stripe within the partner&#39;s organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Global Accenture PDM and other GSI PDMs on building strategy, joint solution development, partner enablement, pipeline development, and deal closure in the EMEA region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Accenture and other GSI counterparts to enable Stripe and partner sales teams on the unique joint value prop, lead account mapping workshops, blitz days, and co-create opportunities together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate and partner with cross-functional resources to support Stripe partner co-sell and GTM activities and create and maintain a long-term, scalable joint GTM model that drives partner and user success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support key deal execution with partners, both pre-sales and post-sales (working with Stripe PSMs, PSEs, SAs, and AEs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support weekly pipeline reviews to ensure pipeline information is thorough and accurate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broker internal resources, tools, references, and investments needed to achieve quarterly goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of technology GTM experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategy, sales, and development experience, working alongside consulting partners or ISVs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process-oriented mindset with desire to solve individual challenges while building for scale in mind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the ability to speak to different functional leadership both internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to both lead and be a team player on cross-functional teams that include technical, sales, product, and support resources from Stripe and the partner. Creative in terms of leveraging resources to drive outsized impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel and be present with partners and sellers in front of our users and prospects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build and execute territory and opportunity-specific plans, in partnership with the Global PDM and other cross-functional resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent ongoing operational hygiene, accurately representing sales and partner activities in Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
