&lt;h2&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe builds financial tools and economic infrastructure for the internet. We’re helping ambitious startups and the world’s most successful companies build products, create new business models, and scale their efforts globally. In pursuit of this mission, the Global Partnerships team develops, executes, and manages partnerships and strategic initiatives that enable Stripe’s product and payments ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategic Payments Partnerships team develops and manages relationships with payment methods and ecosystem partners that enable Stripe’s product strategy and deliver new capabilities to Stripe users. The team executes high-impact, cross-functional initiatives across new products, geographic expansion, user advocacy, and policy. These partnerships materially affect Stripe and the products used by millions of Stripe users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Partner Development Manager to own and grow priority payment method partnerships, with a focus on strategic wallets, buy now, pay later (BNPL) providers, and related payment partners. You will manage day-to-day partner relationships and distribution initiatives, lead defined commercial and product initiatives, and work across Stripe to increase payment method adoption and deliver better experiences for users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires sound commercial judgment, a structured approach to execution, and the ability to bring together internal and external stakeholders with different priorities. You will develop deep expertise in your partners and the payment method ecosystem, using that context to identify opportunities, inform Stripe’s decisions, and execute initiatives that support Stripe’s product and business goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage one or more priority payment method partnerships, with a focus on driving joint initiatives and launching new offerings that benefit Stripe users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage go-to-market strategy and enablement for defined payment method partners, products, and/or geographies, creating and executing plans that increase distribution and adoption across Stripe’s user base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage internal and external stakeholders with varying priorities, driving alignment on shared goals. Ensure methodical partner and deal management rooted in clear milestones, performance metrics, and mutual opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use industry and partner knowledge to inform partnership and product plans, and execute agreements and initiatives that support Stripe’s established strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather input from and coordinate with cross-functional stakeholders, including Risk, Legal, Product, and Engineering, to execute partner initiatives and related product plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Sales, Product Sales, Marketing, and Product Marketing to create enablement resources and drive initiatives that increase payment method adoption within Stripe’s user base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify partner stakeholders who can champion Stripe, educate them on Stripe’s value proposition, and build alignment between Stripe and partner teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring an operationally focused mindset to relationship management by setting clear goals, running tight processes, and proactively identifying opportunities to improve execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;We’re looking for someone who has&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in strategic partnerships, business development, go-to-market growth, corporate development, payments, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning partner relationships, channel or distribution initiatives, and/or cross-functional commercial programs from planning through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading commercial discussions or negotiations using established deal strategies and frameworks, with sound judgment about trade-offs and when to escalate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a product-centric environment with meaningful internal and external dependencies. Experience with payments, payment methods, wallets, BNPL, or financial services is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and operational skills, including the ability to define goals and metrics, manage multiple workstreams, maintain tight processes, and use performance insights to improve execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build credibility and influence internal and external stakeholders across a broad range of functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency and comfort operating in ambiguity, paired with the judgment to seek input, build alignment, and escalate when appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Global Partner Marketing team drives growth by developing and scaling go-to-market programs with Stripe&#39;s most strategic channel, technology, and alliance partners. Working cross-functionally with Sales, Product, and GTM teams, the team builds the infrastructure, enablement, and co-marketing programs that extend Stripe&#39;s reach across the partner ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Online &amp;amp; Regional Events Program Manager, you will build the operating foundation behind Partner Marketing’s online and in-person event portfolio. You’ll turn priorities into repeatable programs, capacity and investment plans, and measurable business outcomes. Working closely with Marketing Operations, regional and global marketing teams, and agency partners, you’ll improve how events are selected, planned, delivered, and evaluated—helping the team scale its impact while making thoughtful trade-offs across resources, timing, and budget.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale repeatable event motions across Partner Marketing’s online and in-person portfolio, including partner-led pre-sales and post-sales workshops, partner enablement programs, and co-sell events. Partner with Marketing Operations to use existing infrastructure and processes where possible, improving efficiency and consistency across programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the measurement and analytical framework for partner events. Identify and quantify high-value opportunities, establish event selection criteria and performance benchmarks, and assess results against defined business outcomes. Diagnose the root causes of underperformance and recommend changes that improve impact, efficiency, and return on investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain a capacity model and integrated editorial calendar for Partner Marketing events. Translate priorities and available resources into a clear execution plan, identify capacity constraints and tradeoffs, and recommend where the team should invest, defer, or scale..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the Partner Marketing events budget and forecasting process, tracking commitments and actual spend, identifying risks early, and maintaining forecast accuracy within 1% accuracy .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate Partner Marketing-led events into regional and global marketing calendars. Coordinate with regional, field, partner, and global marketing teams to align timing, audiences, messaging, and resources; identify conflicts or gaps; and recommend solutions that maximize collective impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and launch a shared-services model for Partner Marketing events. Define the service offering, operating model, intake process, roles, and success measures; support the selection and onboarding of a global agency partner; and drive adoption of the service across the Partner Marketing organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage agency performance and service quality by setting clear briefs, milestones, service-level agreements, and escalation paths. Monitor delivery against agreed standards and recommend process or resourcing improvements when performance falls short.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for an analytical and highly organized program manager who can independently lead complex, cross-functional event programs from planning through measurement. You are comfortable operating through ambiguity, managing several workstreams at once, and using data to identify opportunities, anticipate risks, and recommend improvements. You build trusted relationships across teams, communicate clearly, and balance attention to executional detail with a focus on business impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant experience in B2B event marketing, partner marketing, field marketing, or marketing program management, including online and in-person programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently managing complex, cross-functional programs, including defining timelines, deliverables, dependencies, roles, and success measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, with experience establishing performance benchmarks, evaluating program impact and ROI, diagnosing underperformance, and translating findings into recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing program budgets and forecasts, tracking commitments and actual spend, and identifying financial risks early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build repeatable processes, capacity plans, calendars, or operating models that improve efficiency and execution across multiple programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing agencies or vendors, including developing briefs, setting expectations and milestones, monitoring performance, and resolving delivery issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to align stakeholders across regions, functions, and levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing events or programs for technology, channel, alliance, or ecosystem partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating a shared-services model across multiple teams or regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting global and regional marketing calendars and coordinating programs across AMER, EMEA, and APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with marketing operations, pipeline measurement, event attribution, and CRM or marketing-automation systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

