&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note - for candidates living within 35 miles of a Stripe office (San Francisco, Seattle, New York, Chicago or Georgia) we operate a hybrid work policy where 50% office attendance per month is expected. For candidates more than 35 miles from an office, fully remote work can be approved.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner Solutions Engineering sits within Global Partnerships at the intersection of Stripe’s Product and Engineering teams and the partners that extend Stripe’s platform. We own the partner-side technical outcome for selected partnership work, from architecture and implementation through testing, launch readiness, and production support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Ecosystem Partner Solutions Engineering team helps partners build high-quality integrations across Stripe’s app and developer-platform ecosystem. We work across areas such as developer tools, commerce, billing, automation, and data, while helping Stripe turn recurring partner needs into stronger products and reusable integration paths.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work has two forms. We deliver priority partner implementations, and we turn the lessons from those implementations into Product feedback, reference architectures, testing and certification paths, and reusable guidance. This allows Stripe to support more partners without treating every implementation as a bespoke project.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Partner Solutions Engineer, Ecosystem, you will own the technical outcome for a portfolio of ecosystem areas and priority partner integrations. You will work directly with partners, Partner Development Managers, Product Managers, and Engineers to move opportunities from technical discovery through implementation and launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also develop deep expertise in selected parts of Stripe’s app and developer platform. You will identify recurring technical barriers, help Product teams distinguish isolated partner requests from broader platform needs, and create reusable paths that improve the next partner’s experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, partner-facing engineering role. The strongest candidates can move comfortably between partner architecture, API and code-level debugging, Product feedback, delivery planning, and executive communication.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own partner technical delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical planning, architecture, implementation support, testing, and launch readiness for selected partner integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate partner goals into clear technical requirements, dependencies, milestones, and success criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain one accountable technical plan across the partner, Global Partnerships, Product, and Engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify delivery risks early and drive technical decisions through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead critical partner escalations and help resolve complex production integration failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage an ecosystem portfolio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a technical portfolio across multiple ecosystem areas, based on team priorities and your expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with partnership leads to prioritize integrations and determine where dedicated technical support will create the most value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect partner technical delivery to adoption, commercial, and user outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize technical engagements based on partner impact, strategic value, implementation readiness, and team commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop platform expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop deep expertise in Stripe’s app, developer-platform, and extensibility capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise partners and other Partner Solutions Engineers on embedded experiences, workflow automation, application distribution, permissions, and monetization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain reference architectures, implementation guidance, testing standards, and certification paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track emerging platform capabilities and help priority partners adopt them successfully.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence Stripe’s Product roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring friction and unmet partner needs through direct implementation work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distinguish partner-specific requirements from platform gaps that affect multiple integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate implementation evidence into clear Product requirements and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product and Engineering teams to reach clear decisions on requirements, workarounds, ownership, and sequencing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close the feedback loop with partners when Stripe makes or declines a Product investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create reusable technical leverage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn initial partner builds into repeatable implementation and enablement paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build prototypes, examples, scripts, or lightweight tooling when they accelerate partner delivery or validate a Product direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define launch-readiness standards across permissions, authorization, testing, observability, and production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transition mature integration patterns to scalable support models when they no longer require dedicated engineering ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to shared team standards for custom partner applications, incidents, escalations, and partner handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure outcomes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track technical milestones, launch outcomes, adoption signals, and implementation quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure the commercial, user, or Product outcomes that your work enables, accelerates, or protects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use portfolio data to identify repeated blockers, improve prioritization, and guide future investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. Preferred qualifications are useful but not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in solutions engineering, partner engineering, software engineering, technical consulting, developer relations engineering, or another hands-on technical role supporting external users or partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and delivering production integrations using APIs, webhooks, authentication and authorization, event-driven systems, or developer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read, write, and debug code in at least one general-purpose programming language such as JavaScript or TypeScript, Python, Ruby, Java, or Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience diagnosing complex integration failures across partner systems, APIs, and product surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading external partners from technical discovery through implementation, testing, and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate ambiguous partner goals into a clear architecture, delivery plan, and set of technical decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify patterns across multiple implementations and turn them into reusable guidance or Product requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication with technical, business, and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across Product, Engineering, Partnerships, Sales, or other cross-functional teams without relying on direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment when balancing partner urgency, Product constraints, implementation quality, and long-term platform leverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with developer platforms, platform ecosystems, marketplaces, or partner-distributed products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with application extensibility, embedded applications, workflow automation, OAuth, or delegated API access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments, fintech, commerce, billing, monetization, or financial operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating partner certification, integration-quality, or launch-readiness programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building prototypes, examples, or developer tooling that influenced a Product roadmap or accelerated partner adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch priority partner integrations that produce measurable user, adoption, commercial, or Product outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give partners one accountable technical owner through implementation and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve Stripe’s Products by bringing clear, repeated partner evidence into roadmap decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce repeated partner blockers through reusable architecture, guidance, testing, and certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop recognized expertise across your assigned ecosystem areas and Stripe’s app and developer-platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase the number of partner integrations that can move to scalable support models without sacrificing quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mission of Fraud Operations is to act as guardians of the global financial ecosystem by proactively reducing fraud, making it difficult and unprofitable for fraudsters to carry out attacks through Stripe. Fraud Ops is responsible for developing and maintaining scalable processes related to fraud analysis, card testing, account takeover, and financial partner investigation requests. We strive to improve manual fraud decisioning and enhance support experiences for users impacted by fraud decisions, all while enabling healthy growth for the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Payments Fraud Investigator, you will play a critical role in safeguarding our financial ecosystem by investigating high-risk accounts and identifying various forms of fraud. You will conduct deep-dive analyses of merchant accounts, lead cross-functional projects, and collaborate with stakeholders to enhance our fraud detection and prevention strategies at scale. Your expertise in fraud patterns and typologies will be essential in developing and enhancing investigative processes and programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Analyze high-risk accounts to identify fraudulent merchants, card testing, account takeovers, and other fraud vectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Lead root cause analyses to identify gaps in current systems, policies, and strategies, and determine enhancements and process improvements to address emerging fraud risks through collaboration with key stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Drive cross-functional projects aimed at refining operational processes and tools, enhancing the detection and management of fraudulent accounts across our global analyst network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Investigate, mitigate, and remediate urgent fraud incidents, such as card testing and account takeover, and manage user responses to high-urgency distributed fraud attacks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Communicate regular updates during team and organization-wide business reviews, summarize outcomes of complex investigations for executives, and deliver clear case determinations to users and partner financial institutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Travel to vendor locations to conduct analyst training sessions and knowledge-sharing initiatives, while identifying challenges and enhancing analyst performance to improve overall outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• This role may require weekend coverage as part of an on-call rotation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• 3+ years of experience conducting complex investigations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• 1+ years of experience leading risk-related projects and initiatives, collaborating effectively with cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Demonstrated ability to leverage data to propose solutions for both tactical and strategic challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Proactive approach to challenging the status quo, with a willingness to question existing processes and advocate for improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• User-centric perspective when addressing challenges, balanced with a pragmatic and solutions-oriented mindset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Ability to travel to vendor locations for up to 10% of the year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience in payments, e-commerce, social media, or fintech, mitigating digital or card-not-present fraud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience investigating and mitigating card testing and account takeover attacks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience designing fraud and risk workflows, analyst tooling, and process and procedural workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strong proficiency using SQL to analyze data, drive insights, and create dashboards and visualizations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Payments Performance Team identifies payment optimization opportunities for Stripe’s merchants. The Global Payments Performance team serves a critical role both in demonstrating thought leadership on challenging payment topics, and also partnering with our high-potential merchants to set them up for long term success. We want a partnership with Stripe to be a competitive advantage for our customers, large and small, by providing them with best-in-class technology in concert with insightful and specific advice on how to harness this technology to achieve their business goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Payments Performance Strategist, LatAm, will be responsible for leading data-driven discussions with existing and prospective LatAm merchants on optimisation strategies across a variety of areas including, card network costs, acceptance, fraud, and cross-border flows to start. Initially, the focus will be primarily on the Mexican market.&amp;nbsp; You will be instrumental in building our optimisation narratives/tools and delivering on our merchant engagement model. You will also collaborate with Sales, deploying your knowledge to differentiate Stripe to win deals, and partner with our Customer Success organization to ensure that merchants are successful working with Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as both an internal and merchant-facing expert on payment optimisation strategies in LatAm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with strategic merchants to identify, diagnose, and solve complex payments performance challenges, using quantitative and qualitative analysis to uncover root causes and improvement opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze performance across the end-to-end payments funnel, including authorization, conversion, fraud and risk, payment methods, and cost of payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex payments data and technical concepts into clear, actionable insights and compelling executive-level narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discussions with existing and prospective LatAm merchants from problem definition through recommendation, and provide the Sales team with tools and training to lead discussions with merchants and prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and build on Stripe’s wide-ranging payments expertise to create LatAm optimisation narratives/tools supported by rigorous analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use existing tools to deploy sophisticated optimisation playbooks and analyses across Stripe’s LatAm customer portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify patterns across individual customer engagements and turn bespoke insights into scalable frameworks, tools, playbooks, and best practices to improve our self-serve offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize and relay customer feedback and our findings to inform Stripe’s product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in payments or operations at a leading technology company, or consultancy in the payments industry, with a focus on the LatAm market&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of e-commerce payments, cards based payments processing and optimisation strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting directly to merchants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a subject matter expert providing both internal and customer-facing advisory in the payments domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language proficiency in Spanish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL, dashboard building, modeling, or reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of card network rules and regulations, local payment methods, and the regulatory environment (PSD2/PSD3)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting to senior business leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mission of the People Analytics team is to improve Stripe’s performance by collecting data, measuring critical constructs, and generating insights that help Stripe attract, develop, and retain our most important asset: our Stripes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a team with diverse backgrounds across consulting, HR, and data-focused disciplines who are curious, passionate, and committed to using science and data to deliver high-value, precise outputs to our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of analytics and business partnership in equal measure. You will serve as the People Analytics Analyst and Business Partner to the People Partners supporting Stripe&#39;s International organization who look after our global sites across Core, Tech, and GTM functions. As the sole People Analytics team member based in Europe, you will be the first point of contact for International stakeholders and will need to operate with confidence and autonomy in that capacity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary analytics partner and single point of contact for People Partners and senior business leaders supporting Stripe&#39;s International organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and present comprehensive analyses that shape how leaders understand and act on their organizations, including ad hoc requests requiring urgency and clear communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain analytics products and self-service tooling through Visier and AI-powered solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead backend Visier platform administration including metric and dimension configuration, data hygiene, security, and report design governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with data engineering to identify and execute improvements to our workforce data ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across People Research and Insights, People Partners, and the Business to identify and deliver the highest-impact work&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an analytics analyst and business partner who will help us in our ongoing journey to build a world class People Analytics team and improve the overall employee experience and productivity of our Stripes. You are someone who is curious, has an eye towards craftsmanship and enjoys working in a very fast-paced environment.&amp;nbsp; Through your work, you will likely need to partner closely with our People Research &amp;amp; Insights team, People Partners, People Org teams, and the Business to identify opportunities for greatest impact - then deliver value through creative problem-solving, actionable insights, and effective people practices. Examples of projects this individual may lead include Org health analysis, team size and spans, talent density, recruiting productivity, and geo strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in management consulting, people analytics, or a related analytical role (inside or outside of HR)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate in a business partner capacity, working directly with senior stakeholders as a single point of contact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data visualization and communication skills, with the ability to translate complex findings into clear narratives for a range of audiences including senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Visier or a comparable BI platform; Visier experience strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI platforms such as those from Anthropic, OpenAI, or Google to develop tooling and accelerate analytical workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with human capital benchmarking and target setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity, competing priorities, and delivering high-quality work at pace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting international or multi-site organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across the full analytics project lifecycle from requirements gathering through deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias toward automation, self-service enablement, and building for scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a scripting language such as Python or R&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current on best practices, research, and case studies in people analytics and workforce measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can bring structure to ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One of the key drivers to our success is a committed and rigorous emphasis on our people. We believe that our competitive advantage lies in our talent and that we can build a sustainable advantage by attracting, enabling, and cultivating the world&#39;s most exceptional people to do the very best work of their careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is looking for a People Consultant to join our global team. This Chicago-based role will support Stripe managers and their teams, primarily in the United States and Canada. People Consultants at Stripe enable and support managers to build and lead successful teams. They have deep HR expertise and they leverage policies, experience, insights, and cross-functional partnerships—primarily with other People teams—to guide and coach managers, contribute to a culture of high performance, incrementally improve organizational health, and enable compliant, fair, and positive experiences for Stripes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a People Consultant, you&#39;ll help make Stripe a great place to work and grow. You&#39;ll partner with, coach, enable, and advise Stripe&#39;s people managers on all things people-related, including performance management and coaching, career development, employee relations, leveling, manager effectiveness, navigating change, and more. This is a dynamic role that collaborates with Stripes across all levels, functions, and geographies and is a great opportunity to have an outsized impact on the culture of a fast-moving, scaling, global tech company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manager Coaching:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Provide targeted coaching and consulting to managers at various levels to support their growth and effectiveness across a wide range of people-related topics, including performance management, career development, conflict resolution, and navigating organizational change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HR Policy Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Act as a subject matter expert on a range of HR policies and processes to support managers and employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Legal and Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Work with legal counsel and external consultants to address complex issues and ensure compliance with labor regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Programs:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Support key talent management initiatives such as annual cyclical programs, performance management, workforce reviews, and employee listening to ensure smooth and timely execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reorganization Support:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Guide and advise on change management and communications for team restructuring efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data and Insights:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Analyze people and process data and trends to identify gaps in processes, policies, employee experience, or team dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User Focus:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Ensure excellent employee experiences through key life-cycle stages, including onboarding and departure processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead with Empathy:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Foster a culture of humility, optimism, belonging, and inclusivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–8 years of HR experience, including at least 3 years in a client-facing HR role (e.g., HR Generalist, HR Business Partner, and Employee Relations partner), or equivalent experience in a business-facing role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Manager Support:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Demonstrated experience independently advising and coaching managers at varying levels on performance management, employee relations, and team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Legal Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Working knowledge of employment legislation and practices in the United States, including experience working with legal counsel on complex employee matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Strong ability to diagnose problems using data and develop viable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Actively seek ways to improve processes and demonstrate initiative to gain support for and implement changes that deliver positive impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English, including the ability to communicate clearly and credibly with managers at all levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fast-Paced Environment:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Experience working in a rapidly growing technology company or large organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Knowledge and application of AI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Canadian Employment Practices:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Knowledge of employment legislation and practices in Canada&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Proven project management skills with the ability to engage stakeholders effectively and deliver outcomes on schedule&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facilitation Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Experience facilitating team effectiveness workshops with management teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Delivery Center (SDC) strategy will provide operational leverage and expand Stripe’s portfolio of operational capabilities to support the scaled needs of external users and internal Stripe teams. Stripe’s Global People Operations team will sit within the SDC and is a highly collaborative, cross-functional team that drives key support for the People function. We work with many different teams at Stripe. We are nimble and flexible individuals who can wear many different hats. We don’t mind working through ambiguity and love adding organization to chaos. We believe that success is not defined by any one individual, but by the collective work of the entire team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a People Operations Associate in Mexico City, you’ll be part of the new Centralized Operations team within the Global People Operations organization. You’ll process People transactions, respond to inquiries, maintain accurate People data, and work with teams across Stripe to provide timely and reliable support to Stripes worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process People transactions accurately and on time across the worker lifecycle, including hiring, manager, cost center, team, and location changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to inquiries with clear, accurate, and timely information, escalating complex cases to the appropriate specialist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the accuracy and integrity of People data through careful data entry, audits, and issue resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support employment verification requests, candidate documentation, background checks, and other core operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow standard operating procedures while applying sound judgment to ambiguous cases and protecting sensitive information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Specialized Operations, People Systems, and other teams to resolve issues and provide a consistent experience for Stripes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring issues and suggest practical improvements to workflows, documentation, and team practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate AI fluency by using approved AI and automation tools to support research, analysis, and operational efficiency, while verifying outputs, protecting sensitive data, and applying human judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-4 years of experience in People Operations, Shared Services, Human Resources Information Systems, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills in both &lt;strong&gt;English and Spanish&lt;/strong&gt;, including experience supporting users and collaborating with partners across teams or regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience processing high-volume People transactions or operational requests accurately and within defined service levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across core People processes, such as hiring, worker data changes, organizational changes, employment verification, or offboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing cases or inquiries through a ticketing or case-management system, including escalating issues to the appropriate team. Experience with Salesforce is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying company policies, standard operating procedures, and controls to operational work while using judgment in ambiguous situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling sensitive People data with discretion and following established privacy and data-handling requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with People systems or comparable enterprise platforms. Experience with Workday is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A creative and process-oriented mindset, with an interest in improving workflows and the candidate experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with internal stakeholders in a collaborative, service-oriented environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recruiting depends on systems that work reliably for recruiters, hiring managers, interviewers, and candidates. The Recruiting Systems Operations Administrator helps keep those systems running and improves the support experience around them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work closely with Recruiting Operations, Global People Operations, and People Systems. This role supports a clear division of work between routine service delivery and the system governance, integrations, complex configuration, and strategic work owned by Recruiting Systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working CDMX business hours while partnering across Americas time zones, you’ll manage a defined Tier 2 Recruiting Systems portfolio. You’ll troubleshoot tool issues, resolve requests, track recurring problems, and partner with People Systems on improvements. This hands-on role is well suited to someone who enjoys working across systems, applying sound judgment within established processes, and making complex operations easier for others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and resolve Tier 2 support requests through established channels, maintaining clear requester updates, case records, and handoff notes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot recruiting systems, including DocuSign, Gem, LinkedIn Talent Insights, HackerRank, Harver, BrightHire, Qualtrics, Eightfold, Greenhouse, and related platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process recruiting workflow requests, including assessment updates, job-posting changes, candidate-record updates, approved offer amendments, requisition pooling and unpooling, and requests to keep jobs open temporarily or close inactive jobs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor request volume, aging, service-level expectations, and recurring issues to identify risks and opportunities to improve support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and improve runbooks, templates, knowledge-base content, intake forms, and self-service guidance based on common request patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in release testing, validation, quality reviews, recurring Recruiting operations cycles, and reviews of queue trends, documentation gaps, and operational risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People Systems administrators on releases and support priorities, providing complete handoffs when requests require expertise in areas such as complex configuration, integrations, reporting, privacy, security, policy interpretation, or permissions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in recruiting operations, People operations, service delivery, systems support, customer support, or a similar operations environment, including managing a request queue, ticketing system, or case-management process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to troubleshoot system issues, follow defined processes, document work clearly, and identify when escalation is needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail, organization, follow-through, and the ability to prioritize competing requests while providing clear, timely updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling confidential candidate, recruiting, or employee information with discretion, and comfort learning enterprise systems and working across multiple tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Jira, Salesforce, or a comparable ticketing or case-management tool, and professional fluency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Greenhouse or another applicant tracking system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting recruiting technology such as BrightHire, LinkedIn Recruiter, LinkedIn Talent Insights, GoodTime, Gem, HackerRank, DocuSign, Qualtrics, Harver, or Eightfold&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Recruiting Operations, Talent Acquisition Coordination, People Systems, or software-as-a-service administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting offer processes, job-posting management, interview operations, or recruiter onboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating or maintaining standard operating procedures, runbooks, and knowledge articles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic spreadsheet, reporting, or data-quality skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with service-level agreements, queue metrics, audit controls, or release testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spanish fluency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-success-looks-like-in-your-first-six-months&quot;&gt;What success looks like in your first six months&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage your Tier 2 support portfolio with prompt resolutions and clear status updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide reliable coverage across Americas time zones and set transparent escalation expectations for recruiters and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve standard issues across DocuSign, Gem, LinkedIn Talent Insights, HackerRank, Harver, and Greenhouse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate Tier 3 requests to the correct People Systems owner with complete context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate ticket records, handoffs, runbooks, and knowledge-base guides that improve self-service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the reliability of recruiting technology for recruiters, hiring managers, interviewers, and candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the platform knowledge needed to take on additional approved support responsibilities over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Delivery Center (SDC) strategy will provide operational leverage and expand Stripe’s portfolio of operational capabilities to support the scaled needs for external users and internal Stripe teams. Stripe’s People &amp;amp; Places Operations team will sit within the SDC and is a highly collaborative, cross-functional team that drives key support for the People and Places function. We work with many different teams at Stripe. We are nimble and flexible individuals that can wear many different hats. We don’t mind working through ambiguity and love adding organization to chaos. We believe that success is not defined by any one individual, but rather by the collective work of the entire team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic and operational leadership for the newly-formed People Support team in CDMX, translating the global Core Ops strategy into an effective local operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a small team People Support specialists through clear expectations, regular coaching, actionable feedback, and quality calibration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish local team practices, coverage, escalation paths, and ways of working that integrate effectively with the global People Support organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage daily operations, including queue health, workload allocation, service levels, and escalations, while contributing directly during the team’s ramp or periods of high volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use service metrics, case trends, and feedback to set priorities, identify root causes, and improve workflows, documentation, and the user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People, People Systems, and specialist teams to clarify ownership, improve handoffs, and implement global initiatives locally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high standards for case handling, written responses, documentation, data accuracy, privacy, and operational controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to expand the CDMX team’s capabilities and use AI tools thoughtfully to improve service quality, operational efficiency, and the team’s ability to scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic and operational leadership, including the ability to establish new team practices while contributing directly to service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people leadership, coaching, communication, and stakeholder-management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and attention to detail when handling complex or ambiguous People matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze operational data, identify patterns, set priorities, and turn insights into practical improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI fluency, including the ability to use AI tools appropriately, assess output quality, protect sensitive data, and recognize when human review is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6-8 years of experience in People operations, shared services, support operations, or a related field, including 2+ years leading or managing others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A graduate or postgraduate qualification in human resources or a related discipline, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing or developing a new team, service, location, or operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing case queues, escalations, service levels, and operational quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading operational improvements or implementing global initiatives within a local team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with People systems and case-management tools, such as Workday or comparable platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of core People processes, including worker data, benefits, talent mobility, equity, compensation, and exits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance immediate operational needs with longer-term team development and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a technology company focused on improving the conditions for economic growth and prosperity. We build programmable financial infrastructure, rethinking from first principles how financial services should work, to make it easier and cheaper for any business to start and scale. More than 10 million &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers&quot;&gt;businesses&lt;/a&gt; build on Stripe, spanning the economic frontier—from solo founders to established enterprises—united by a practical focus on growth. The most ambitious companies in the world use Stripe as core infrastructure to grow faster. They process trillions of dollars a year on Stripe, equivalent to around 1.6% of global GDP. While economic growth makes everyone better off, open markets also enable greater variety. When any business can easily serve a global customer base, the quality and diversity of products in the world increase, and craft and creativity are unleashed into the smallest niches. Our own growth is wholly contingent on the success of the businesses building on Stripe. We therefore invest back into our technology at an unusual rate. We make &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/roadmap&quot;&gt;upgrades to our products&lt;/a&gt; every single day to deliver compounding gains to our customers. We maintain some of the most &lt;a href=&quot;https://status.stripe.com/&quot;&gt;reliable APIs&lt;/a&gt; on the internet. We build entirely new &lt;a href=&quot;https://tempo.xyz/&quot;&gt;pieces&lt;/a&gt; of &lt;a href=&quot;https://mpp.dev/&quot;&gt;financial&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://joinopenstandard.com/&quot;&gt;infrastructure&lt;/a&gt; to enable new ideas. And our significant advances in &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/radar&quot;&gt;risk and fraud&lt;/a&gt; infrastructure over many years are making the internet economy safer and more accessible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Though people at Stripe don’t tend to take themselves seriously, Stripe is a fairly serious place: our customers are depending on us for their livelihoods. We admire ambition, intensity, curiosity, humility, and rigor. The most effective people become knowledgeable about many domains besides their own. Any company is an applied exercise in understanding some aspect of society or the market. In working with so many (especially the new and innovative ones), we think that Stripe is one of the very best places to learn about how the world works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Data Science team partners deeply with teams across Stripe to ensure that our users, our products, and our business have the models, data products, and insights needed to make decisions and grow responsibly. We&#39;re looking for data scientists with a passion for analyzing data, building machine learning and statistical models, and running experiments to drive impact. Our Fraud, Losses, and Financial Crime Data Science team builds the models and data products that protect Stripe and its users from fraud, account takeover, and financial crime. We own the full fraud and loss modeling stack - from account takeover detection and card fraud classification to merchant-level loss estimation, unsupervised anomaly detection, and financial crime risk modeling. We partner with Fraud Engineering, Financial Crimes Engineering, and Risk Operations to bring these systems into production and ensure they have measurable impact on Stripe&#39;s financial integrity and user trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an intern at Stripe you’ll work on projects across our stack that directly impact the way millions of businesses operate. You’ll own problems end to end with the support of your manager and teammates. It’s an opportunity to work alongside some of the most creative and technically rigorous data analysts and scientists in the industry. You&#39;ll partner deeply with teams across Stripe to ensure that our users, our products, and our business have the models, data products, and insights needed to make decisions and grow responsibly. You&#39;ll work closely with partners to extract insights from the rich and complex data at Stripe. You&#39;ll build metrics, scalable data pipelines, dashboards, and reports to inform and run the business. You&#39;ll deliver actionable business recommendations through analyses and data storytelling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our internship program is competitive and the expectations are high.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applying probability distributions, statistical inference, and hypothesis testing to quantify uncertainty and evaluate business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using Python or R for data analysis, data processing, visualizations, statistical modeling, machine learning, predictive analytics, automation, and implementing causal inference and experimental analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building, training, and evaluating predictive models across regression and classification tasks for bias-variance trade-offs and model selection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modeling temporal dependencies, seasonality, and trend decomposition to generate and evaluate time-series predictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying structural patterns, clusters, and outliers in unlabeled data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploying models in production and adjusting model thresholds to improve performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing, running, and analyzing complex experiments and leveraging causal inference designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using SQL and Spark to create, transform, and analyze large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn quickly by asking great questions, finding how to work with your mentor and teammates effectively, and communicating the status of your work clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present your work to the Data Science team, partner teams, and fellow interns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ambitious builder: You’re energized by building solutions without clear precedent and solving problems with far-reaching consequences. Successful Stripes are deeply curious, and prefer the joy of discovery to the comfort of certainty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigorous thinker: You appreciate that things worth doing are rarely simple. You enjoy working on problems that have never been tackled before.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable problem solver: You adapt quickly and treat obstacles as opportunities. At Stripe we embrace kindness while encouraging Stripes to take measured risks and act boldly, even in the absence of consensus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enrolled in a quantitative &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;PhD program&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (e.g. Data Science, Statistics, Economics, Mathematics, etc.) with the expectation of graduating in December 2027 or spring/summer 2028&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL and a scientific computing language (such as Python, R, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with AI tools to accelerate model development, analysis, and coding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience communicating and collaborating with multidisciplinary stakeholders in a team environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing and debugging data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to evaluate and receive feedback from mentors, peers, and stakeholders via experience from previous internships or other multi-person projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn new systems and form an understanding of those systems, through independent research and working with a mentor and subject matter experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

