&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Executive Content &amp;amp; Experiences team builds trusted relationships with leaders shaping the global economy. We design high-impact programs—including executive briefings, advisory boards, flagship convenings at Davos, and executive programming at Stripe Sessions—to bring Stripe&#39;s strategy to life. Beyond delivering premier high-touch moments, we turn leadership insights into actionable intelligence that directly informs Stripe’s narratives, product, and go-to-market direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a rock star product marketer to translate Stripe’s most complex technology and strategy into compelling, executive-ready narratives and scalable sales motions. In this role, you will lead the content strategy and enablement engine that powers our highest-stakes executive moments—from global Executive Briefing Centers (EBCs) to bespoke leadership workshops. Sitting at the intersection of Product, Sales, and Executive Engagement, you will equip Stripe leaders, account teams, and event hosts to clearly articulate Stripe as the complete financial infrastructure for the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop Thought Leadership Narratives: Craft tailored, point-of-view-driven narratives and presentations for executive-level meetings, advisory boards, and Tier-1 convenings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Executive Briefing Center Enablement: Develop and scale sales enablement frameworks, messaging toolkits, and prep materials to empower account teams to lead impactful executive briefings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Scalable Workshop Motions: Architect and scale interactive whiteboarding and workshop frameworks that simplify complex product architectures and showcase Stripe as a complete financial infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curate Executive Demo Library: Build, maintain, and package an executive-ready demo library—repurposing existing product assets into high-touch formats designed specifically for executive experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Speaker Training &amp;amp; Certification: Create and scale a formal speaker training and certification program to prepare Stripe executives and technical subject matter experts for high-profile speaking roles and EBC engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale Content via AI: Design and deploy AI agents and workflows to automate content generation, personalize executive materials, and streamline enablement at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A crisp storyteller, strategic thinker, and enablement innovator. You are a sharp, driven problem-solver with a relentless bias for action—someone who isn&#39;t afraid to get scrappy and is energized by building new capabilities for growing teams. You excel at taking deep technical complexity—like global payments infrastructure and financial software—and turning it into elegant, high-impact stories for C-suite audiences. You understand how executive sales motions work and know how to build repeatable systems, scalable tools, and AI-driven workflows that elevate an entire organization’s narrative capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of product marketing, solutions marketing, or executive enablement experience in B2B tech, SaaS, or fintech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record building executive-level narratives and high-touch customer workshop motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing and executing sales enablement programs, speaker training, or certification frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and visual communication skills, with extensive experience presenting to and prepping C-suite leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success working cross-functionally across Product, Sales, and Field Marketing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Pricing Strategy team is part of the Stripe Product Marketing organization and is responsible for how Stripe prices its products. Our work is highly cross-functional and we partner closely with Product, Finance, and Sales to tackle some of the most visible and commercially impactful decisions at Stripe. We&#39;re looking for someone who blends financial analysis, strategic thinking, and stakeholder engagement to help us price new products and evaluate their pricing performance as the products evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the center of the Stripe pricing architecture, working horizontally across our product portfolio to shape how Stripe packages and prices its suite of products. Rather than going deep on a single product, you&#39;ll develop the frameworks, methodologies, and strategic recommendations that govern how our products work together commercially. Your work will be highly visible to Stripe leadership and directly shape how millions of businesses experience the value of Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the frameworks, methodologies, and strategies that govern how Stripe products are priced and packaged together commercially, aligned to our long-term commercial goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize the value of the Stripe product portfolio through qualitative research, competitive benchmarking, and willingness-to-pay analysis to inform cross-product packaging decisions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build financial models to evaluate the impact of pricing changes on revenue, margin, and user behavior&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive alignment across Finance, Legal, Product, and Go-to-Market stakeholders on pricing architecture decisions and bring them to execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain internal pricing enablement resources — playbooks, frameworks, and processes — that help the broader pricing organization operate more effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–7 years of relevant experience in an operational role or in a management consultancy, ideally delivering Pricing, Go-to-Market, or Product recommendations, or working on highly strategic questions for the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting qualitative and quantitative user research on product needs and value perceptions, as well as market research and competitive benchmarking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, and a willingness to proactively work with functions across the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to ask the right questions and to use sound business judgment when collaborating with a wide range of stakeholders&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the payments ecosystem and value chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to maintain high performance under tight timelines, and a hands-on mindset to get any job done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL or AI tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe, you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach. Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;careers-listing-details__body&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;hds-text careers-listing-details__body-content hds-text--md hds-text--soft&quot;&gt;
&lt;article&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Specialist Solutions Architects (SSA) are domain experts aligned to specific Stripe solutions and customer buying centers. We have in-depth knowledge of specific solution offerings and a deep understanding of customer challenges. We align with specialist product sellers on deals, advise the broader pre-sales team on complex opportunities, support pipeline development and revenue attainment, serve as an advisor on go-to-market sales plays, and provide critical insights to our product and engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/article&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Specialist Solution Architect, you will lead in-depth product discussions with our top users and prospects and execute against our go-to-market strategy for our Money Management products, including Stripe Capital, Issuing, Treasury, and our global Payouts suite. You will educate our product and engineering teams on market trends and strongly influence the product roadmap for the Money Management product suite at Stripe, helping us become the primary way merchants run their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert on Stripe’s Money Management products (including Capital, Issuing, Treasury, and our global Payouts suite) to accelerate opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate a deep understanding of embedded finance applications that leverage Stripe’s products, articulating how they combine to create a compounding platform for our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult with users on a broad range of embedded finance use cases, from charge card programs and global payouts to a comprehensive suite of financing options including revenue-based financing, loans, and lines of credit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the compliance requirements of solutions built with Stripe products, especially as we expand our offerings into new markets and use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, share, and learn best practices and reusable assets with the broader GTM organization to enhance the quality and efficiency of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create reference architectures to uplevel the team and refine reference solutions based on product enhancements and feedback from customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Money Management product sales team and be an active part of the opportunity team for Stripe’s largest customers to lead strategy and own key relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a “Voice of the Customer” internally, providing actionable insights to product stakeholders to influence the Money Management product roadmap and feature prioritization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide critical insights on emerging technologies, including the application of stablecoins for money movement, lending, and global financial access, to influence the product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand the sales process for the product and provide the Sales team with tools and training to qualify potential leads, including simplifying our distribution for faster onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on competitive analysis and market differentiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support marketing events including executive briefings, conferences, user groups, and trade shows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in a technical sales, pre-sales, or solutions architecture role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of product experience with embedded finance solutions, such as card issuing, lending, or treasury management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with integrating RESTful APIs into web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills, comfortable explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for learning and researching current and emerging products to develop innovative solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to deal effectively with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of software engineering and architecture patterns, with the ability to understand how a wide variety of technologies and systems interact with each other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience enabling and scaling a GTM team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in systems design, with a background building and deploying complex applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Pricing Strategy team is part of Stripe&#39;s Product Marketing organization and is responsible for how Stripe prices its products. Our work is highly cross-functional and we partner closely with Product Management, Finance, and Sales to tackle some of Stripe&#39;s most visible and commercially impactful decisions. We&#39;re looking for someone who can blend financial analysis, strategic thinking, stakeholder engagement, and operational rigor to help us price new products and evaluate their pricing performance as the products evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will support the development and execution of pricing and packaging strategies across Stripe’s existing and upcoming products. Working at the intersection of Product development, Go-to-Market, and financial planning, you will analyze pricing questions, develop recommendations, and help cross-functional teams move from insight to execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also play an important role in strengthening how the Pricing Strategy team operates - bringing structure and consistency to recurring processes, improving visibility into the team’s work, and identifying opportunities to help the team scale and increase impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an understanding of the value Stripe’s products deliver to users and how they compare with relevant alternatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive alignment across Finance, Legal, Product, and Go-to-Market stakeholders on pricing proposals and bring them to execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage internal and research data to build financial models to evaluate the impact of pricing changes on revenue, margin, and user behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to scalable tools and processes that help the Pricing Strategy team work more consistently and efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of relevant experience in pricing, strategy, operations, finance, product, or management consulting, ideally involving pricing, go-to-market, product recommendations, or other strategic business questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting qualitative and quantitative user research on product needs and value perceptions, as well as market research and competitive benchmarking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, and a willingness to proactively work with functions across the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to ask the right questions and to use sound business judgment when collaborating with a wide-range of stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the payments ecosystem and value chain, knowledge of software and AI industry pricing model and trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to maintain high performance under tight timelines, and a “roll up your sleeves” mindset to get any job done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data acumen and background in data and/or financial analysis preferred, SQL or AI experience a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Privacy Operations team is a pivotal part of the global privacy program at Stripe. Our vision is operational excellence—a team that is proactive, streamlined, and deeply embedded in the way Stripe works. Privacy Operations is the authoritative operational hub for privacy processes, enabling high-quality privacy experiences for users and data subjects, and owning clear and auditable documentation for internal stakeholders and external regulators. We partner with Privacy Legal and Privacy Engineering to protect user data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll own the programs central to how Stripe handles privacy at scale. You&#39;ll drive end-to-end management across data subject requests, privacy impact assessments, records of processing activities, transfer impact assessments, and cookie compliance, making day-to-day decisions that keep operations regulatory-ready and auditable. You&#39;ll also identify where processes can be tightened or automated, and build the documentation and tooling that make the team&#39;s work consistent and sustainable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work as a key connector between Privacy Legal, Privacy Engineering, and cross-functional partners across the company, translating global privacy requirements into practical operations. As a primary point of contact for incoming privacy requests, you&#39;ll handle triage and routing, and build the playbooks and response libraries that allow the team to deliver high-quality, consistent privacy experiences for Stripe users and for the regulators who depend on clear, auditable records.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end program management across core privacy programs such as data subject requests (DSRs), PIAs and DPIAs, records of processing activities (ROPA), transfer impact assessments (TIAs), and cookie compliance, making day-to-day operational decisions, enforcing processes to ensure regulatory readiness, and measuring compliance at scale&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement process improvements, including leveraging AI tooling to automate routine tasks, developing structured workflows to sustain quality standards, and maintaining accurate, auditable program records including playbooks and process documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain clear, auditable privacy documentation, including privacy assessments, program playbooks, and customer response libraries, to provide scalable, consistent privacy operational support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Privacy Legal and Privacy Engineering to fulfill user requests, build and deepen expertise on global privacy and data-protection requirements, and escalate novel or complex requests with appropriate context and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rotate through the team&#39;s weekly runner model as the primary point of contact for incoming privacy requests, routing across intake channels and managing Jira run tickets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of demonstrated privacy program management and a proven track record of operationalising and scaling cross-functional organisation-wide programs from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent collaboration, communication, and relationship-building skills, and the ability to convey complex ideas succinctly to all audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with privacy legislation such as GDPR, CCPA, LGPD, and PIPEDA. Experience with US state legislation, HIPAA, and GLBA is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with privacy impact assessments (PIAs and DPIAs), data subject request workflows, records of processing activities (ROPA), or other core privacy program operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze complex problems to identify root causes and trends, and to document complex narratives in a simplified way that others can use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and self-motivated with a strong affinity for vision setting, strategic problem solving, and driving outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in juggling multiple projects in a fast-paced, high-growth environment, with tight timelines and shifting priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team player, willing to pitch in where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fast-paced, high-growth environments. Previous tech industry experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience using AI to accelerate day-to-day privacy operations work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with third-party risk management, RFP and DDQ response processes, or cross-border transfer assessments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Privacy certification such as CIPP/E, CIPP/US, or CIPM is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Accounting team at Stripe supports products across Stripe by providing guidance on accounting implications and enabling teams to make informed strategic decisions. The team records business transactions accurately and on time in the balance sheet and income statement, and partners with cross-functional and international teams in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the Product Accounting team to support revenue accounting for Payments and Payment Products. You&#39;ll use your technical expertise in US GAAP, including ASC 606, to identify accounting implications and customer impacts, advise cross-functional partners, and develop operating processes that help Stripe scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable accounting processes to support global growth in payment processing accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, go-to-market, and Finance teams to understand new products, features, and contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Systems and Engineering teams to improve financial systems and automate accounting processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the effectiveness of internal controls and design processes and controls for emerging business activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain current accounting procedure documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and perform monthly and quarterly close activities, including journal entries, balance-sheet reconciliations, variance analyses, financial reporting deliverables, and reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce management analyses and reporting, and support external audit processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 - 4 years of relevant accounting experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional accountancy qualification, such as CA, CPA, ACA, ACCA, or CIMA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with monthly or quarterly close processes, journal-entry preparation and posting, audits, regulatory reporting, financial-statement preparation, and accounting systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of US GAAP, including ASC 606, and experience with internal controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to structure ambiguous work, solve problems using Excel, build systems and automation, collaborate across functions and cultures, and adapt to changing requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the technology or payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Oracle Suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data-querying and analysis tools, including SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data-analysis tools, such as Power BI, Tableau, KNIME, Python, or Alteryx&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Bridge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re creating an entirely new payments platform, built with stablecoins, to simplify global money movement. Bridge enables faster, cheaper payments and borderless access to dollars via stablecoins. Through our APIs, businesses can send and receive funds across borders faster / cheaper vs. SWIFT and other fiat-only rails. Our virtual accounts enable international consumers and businesses to easily access, store and spend US dollars. Our payouts infrastructure enables platforms to disburse USD to anyone globally. We believe many trillions of dollars will move and settle through stablecoin payment rails. Bridge is pulling this future forward.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a small team of people who have previously built financial infrastructure at some of the world’s leading companies (Coinbase, Stripe, Square, Brex, Upstart, DoorDash, Airbnb) and each and every one of them chose Bridge because they fundamentally believe that stablecoins will be a critical piece of financial infrastructure that allows for the improvement of global money movement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Product Analyst&amp;nbsp; to join our Data team at Bridge. You&#39;ll own the data strategy for customer experience at Bridge, spanning two closely linked areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Payments quality&lt;/strong&gt; — transaction speed, uptime/reliability, error rates, and support ticket trends across our payment rails and products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product experience&lt;/strong&gt; — how customers interact with Bridge&#39;s dashboard, onboarding flows, and other surfaces, and where friction is costing us adoption or trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This focus area may shift over time as the business evolves, and we&#39;re looking for someone who can adapt their scope accordingly — spinning up their knowledge of different product areas, creating new analyses and instrumentation as priorities emerge or change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;This is a high-ownership seat: you&#39;ll be the primary data voice for your focal area, expected to identify what matters, build the pipelines and analysis to prove it, and drive decisions from insight through to shipped outcomes — with real latitude to define how you get there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the data needs for your focal area end-to-end: define and refine the right metrics, build the pipelines to source them, and drive them into decisions — without needing significant hand-holding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze payments quality signals (latency, uptime, failure/error rates, support ticket volume and themes) to identify where customers are experiencing friction and quantify the business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze product and UX data (dashboard usage, onboarding funnels, feature adoption) to find opportunities to improve the customer journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain robust, well-documented data pipelines and ETL processes that make customer experience data easy to access, trust, and query across the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain production-quality SQL and pipeline code in Databricks, with work version-controlled and reviewed via GitHub.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain dashboards and self-serve tools that let Product, Engineering, and Support teams monitor customer experience metrics without depending on ad hoc requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, and Support/Operations to translate findings into concrete product and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively flag emerging issues or trends in payments quality or product experience before they become customer-facing problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve data quality, documentation, and tooling for your focal area as Bridge&#39;s product and scale evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience as a data analyst or in a similar analytics role, ideally at a payments, fintech, or high-growth technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent SQL skills, with experience querying and modeling data in a modern warehouse/lakehouse environment (e.g., Databricks).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building and maintaining data pipelines and ETL processes, and comfort working with version control (GitHub) as part of a technical workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and diagnostic skills — able to independently investigate a problem, identify root cause, and turn findings into a clear recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building dashboards and visualizations that communicate insights clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work independently, take ownership of a focal area, and manage multiple concurrent priorities with minimal oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain technical or data-driven findings to non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience analyzing payments data specifically (transaction quality, uptime/reliability, support ticket trends) or product/UX data (onboarding, dashboard engagement, funnels).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming experience (e.g., Python) and familiarity with data manipulation libraries (e.g., pandas).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a fast-paced startup or high-growth environment where priorities and scope shift with the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Communications team builds and protects Stripe’s brand and influence across the world. Product Comms is a team of creative thinkers and entrepreneurial strategists tasked with deepening the understanding of Stripe’s products. We work closely with the Product, Marketing, Policy and wider Comms teams to produce imaginative and effective messaging and provide strategic counsel to our executive team that goes far beyond the bounds of traditional comms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is to lead global product communications for Stripe’s crypto offerings. You’ll work shoulder-to-shoulder with senior leaders and the teams building Stripe’s crypto products to shape the storytelling strategy around this new frontier of financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Three important dimensions of this role include: (i) entrepreneurialism — you’ll work in uncharted territory, building a new comms muscle for Stripe. It’ll be up to you to identify and go after the best opportunities. (ii) superb writing and storytelling — you’ll bring your writing skills to bear on Stripe’s highest profile public moments, such as company letters, executive keynotes, and other long-form content. The vision for Stripe’s crypto products needs to come to life with your words. (iii) attention to detail — building in a new space requires a foundation of trust and legitimacy. You’ll work at an uncompromising quality bar where no detail is too small to matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead global product communications for Stripe’s crypto products,including Bridge and Privy (crypto infrastructure companies acquired by Stripe in 2025).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development, articulation and testing of Stripe’s long-term public vision for its crypto products, specifically as a substrate for economic growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and roll out strategic campaigns that build awareness for Stripe’s crypto products and deepen key audiences’ understanding of exactly what makes stablecoins so useful to global businesses of all sizes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and edit extremely high quality written materials for Stripe’s biggest moments, including newsroom posts, social content, industry keynotes, top tier media interviews and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with local and regional comms leads to raise awareness for Stripe globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain relationships with thought leaders and influencers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic counsel to our executive team, including Stripe’s founders and most senior product leaders, and collaborate closely with your counterparts on the partnerships, policy, and product marketing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve done exceptional work in your career to date and have the proof points to show for it (built a great product, ran a high-impact campaign, started your own business, or similar accomplishments).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a superlative writer; someone who has been recognized by their peers as a truly exceptional writer, with a particular knack for making technically sophisticated topics interesting and memorable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience collaborating effectively with large, cross-functional teams as well as working with senior executives 1:1.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve worked in a technology, B2B and/or financial services or banking environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re passionate about the potential for (and real-world impact of) crypto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re deeply immersed in the world of independent media—Substackers, podcasters, video makers, influencers on X. You might personally know some of the people shaping these conversations (or even be one yourself), but more importantly, you understand the culture, the discourse, and where the zeitgeist is heading next. You combine the best of what you’ve found online with your original ideas to create compelling stories and new insights. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Counsel, Money Movement Legal (Asia-Pacific)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Legal team at Stripe manages the legal and regulatory aspects of designing, building, and launching products and services. The team works on technical, commercial, and regulatory matters and advises product, engineering, and partnerships teams on issues across financial services, business, and technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role supports the Money Movement and Storage business across Asia-Pacific. The business includes stored-value and e-money, foreign exchange, cross-border transfer, stablecoin and digital asset, and other financial products. The team helps ensure these products comply with applicable laws and regulations while supporting responsible product development and commercialization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Product Counsel, you&#39;ll advise teams on the legal and regulatory considerations for money movement products across Asia-Pacific. You&#39;ll partner with product, engineering, partnerships, compliance, risk, marketing, and Legal teams to navigate emerging requirements and bring products to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the Product Legal team deliver products that comply with laws and contractual commitments to users globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise product teams on the intersection of technological innovation, e-commerce user experiences, and financial services compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product, engineering, partnerships, compliance, risk, and marketing teams on product development and commercialization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise teams on new and emerging legal and regulatory developments, identify potential effects on business activities, and apply existing laws to new technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with colleagues across the global Legal team to support regulatory structures, customer agreements, and strategic financial partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and build scalable processes for legal review and product launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up to date on money movement laws and regulations, and serve as a strategic advisor to senior managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience as a qualified lawyer in a law firm, in-house legal team, or government agency, with expertise in payment services laws and regulations, such as the Payment Services Act of Singapore&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualification to practice law, preferably in a jurisdiction in Asia-Pacific&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising technology teams and translating complex legal requirements into clear, actionable advice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate with teammates, share knowledge, understand complex business models and product use cases, and exercise sound judgment with imperfect information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication, project management, and prioritization skills in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on the development of stablecoin and digital asset products, particularly across multiple regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting legal, regulatory, or commercial matters for money movement or financial services products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a part of the Connect Design team, you&#39;ll lead product development for the largest complex users on Stripe—marketplaces such as Doordash and Lyft, and platforms such as Shopify and Woo. You&#39;ll drive the vision for how these marketplaces and platforms manage risk and compliance for their business and their users in the US and internationally. You&#39;ll work with other designers on the team to define the future of the experience for all Connect users on the dashboard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll utilize a broad set of product design skills including user interface design, user experience and interaction design, and prototyping. In this role, you&#39;ll be responsible for deeply understanding our users and product strategy to design and advocate for the highest quality product experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;em&gt;Connect Risk product design team&lt;/em&gt; creates experiences that help platforms and marketplaces identify, understand, and manage risk across their connected accounts. The team works on tools that protect platforms from fraud and credit losses while giving them visibility and control over risk operations—including account reviews, risk controls, fraud insights, underwriting, reserves, and the ability to pause payments or payouts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Designing for Connect Risk means supporting two distinct audiences: the platforms managing risk and the connected businesses affected by risk decisions. The work spans onboarding, verification, ongoing monitoring, interventions, remediation, and support across Stripe-hosted, embedded, and API-based experiences. Designers must make complex risk decisions understandable and actionable while balancing loss prevention, regulatory and technical constraints, platform control, and a low-friction user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end product design process from discovery through delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship meaningful, high-quality experiences that balance business needs with usability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering, product, and other stakeholders to shape the team&#39;s roadmap and goals from an impactful and measurable customer outcomes perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage insights from our UXR team to identify opportunity areas, and to validate potential solutions to pain points&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with content design to craft compelling experiences that deliver the right information at the right time to the right user&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with other product designers to drive holistic solutions for our marketplaces and platforms and their users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re a product designer who thrives in complex, interconnected problem spaces. You bring strong design fundamentals and polished UI craft, quickly develop informed perspectives, and translate user needs, business goals, and technical constraints into thoughtful solutions. You’re proactive and self-directed, comfortable navigating ambiguity and shared ownership, and skilled at influencing cross-functional teams through clear storytelling. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has 6+ years relevant design experience at a tech, product-driven company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has experience working in a complex problem space such as B2B or SaaS interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio that demonstrates strong design fundamentals and polished UI craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with cross-functional teams to shape product direction and proven ability to influence teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance user needs, business goals, and multiple stakeholder inputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working horizontally across product areas on ambiguous and complex problems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident presenting work to company leadership and skilled at communicating design decisions through a clear and compelling story&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are skilled in explaining your work, process, and decisions to cross-functional stakeholders and crave feedback to help you produce your best work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Care about details and are excited to keep pushing your work until it is pixel-perfect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Value working with a diverse group of people with different perspectives and expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love working with other designers to help them learn and grow—and have them help you learn and grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are committed to building a sustainable and scalable business by balancing user and business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Design team is made up of several groups that define, create, and deliver all user-facing aspects of the Stripe brand and product. Product Designers are strategic partners to Engineering and Product Management within their product area. In close collaboration with product teams, they shape user experiences, then translate them into high-quality designs that can be tested, shipped, and refined. Designers are responsible for building elegant, functional products that users love—and want to tell others about.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Dashboard team ensures Stripe works seamlessly for every merchant—regardless of how their business is structured or which products they use. Our goal is to make Stripe feel like it was built just for them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will help build and enhance the Stripe Dashboard by designing, concepting, and prototyping high-quality core dashboard and product experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the Stripe ecosystem, users, and UI to inform product direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver high-quality, user-centered designs that evolve core surfaces and elevate the overall user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with designers, product managers, engineers, user researchers, and content designers to shape strategy and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share work regularly in design reviews and actively contribute to a strong culture of feedback and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years relevant design experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio showcasing strong design skills with high-quality, well-crafted UI experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with product, engineering, and other cross-functional teams to drive product direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work horizontally across product verticals and collaborate upwards with team and company leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to wrangle lots of competing priorities, points of view, as well as user and business needs to come up with a solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience designing for a B2B or fintech product&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sail is Stripe’s user interface platform and design system. We build the design language, components, tools, and front-end foundations that product teams use to create coherent, accessible, responsive, and high-quality experiences. Designers on Sail work closely with engineers and designers across Stripe to turn recurring product needs into durable solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Designer on Sail, you’ll contribute to the visual and interaction foundations of Stripe’s products. With support from experienced designers and engineers, you’ll work on scoped components, patterns, guidance, and tools. This role is a good fit for a designer who cares deeply about visual craft, enjoys thinking in systems, and wants to understand how design decisions become production interfaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and refine user interface components, patterns, and foundations for use across Stripe products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create polished, coherent interfaces across interaction states, themes, and responsive layouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with front-end engineers to understand constraints and carry designs into production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Figma libraries, prototypes, specifications, documentation, and examples&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather input from product teams, share work, and iterate based on feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience designing digital products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio demonstrating strong visual design craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using or contributing to a design system or component library&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with front-end engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working understanding of components, states, and responsive behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using artificial intelligence tools in day-to-day design work, with familiarity with large language models, agents, and reusable skills or workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating or maintaining user interface components or shared design libraries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of HTML and CSS, with experience using artificial intelligence and prototyping tools to build and evaluate interactive interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing native mobile interfaces for iOS or Android&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Design team is made up of several groups that define, create, and deliver all user-facing aspects of Stripe&#39;s products. Product Designers work directly with Engineers, Product Managers, Data Scientists, and Marketers, as strategic partners, in each product area. In close collaboration with product teams, they shape user experiences, then translate them into high-quality designs that can be tested, shipped, and refined. Designers are responsible for building elegant, functional products that users love—and want to tell others about.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global design team crafts product experiences that make cross-border selling as simple, performant, and scalable as domestic sales. Experiences empower businesses to easily expand into new markets worldwide without the friction of complex global operations, ranging from localized checkout experiences and comprehensive payment method coverage to handling global tax compliance and cross-border money management. Because of its global reach, this team&#39;s efforts drive significant impact for our users and business and navigate the unique challenges of designing for regions with dozens of currencies, languages, and regulatory frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a product designer, you&#39;ll work closely with product managers and engineering teams to envision features in the Stripe Dashboard and checkout surfaces and partner with go-to-market teams to bring them to users. That includes new feature development, localization for priority geographies across Europe, the Middle East, and Africa, and setting vision for our products to meet new user expectations in an increasingly globally connected and AI-driven world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user workflows and pain points, and produce, test, and iterate on high-quality designs to solve user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product, engineering, marketing, and strategy partners to define a north star and product experience for new features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype user experiences for user research testing and internal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with teams across Stripe to craft a seamless dashboard user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct UXR to test design decisions before shipping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with our design systems teams to leverage and improve templates and components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of relevant design experience at a product-driven tech company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong craft demonstrated through a portfolio of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated skills in prototyping at high fidelity using the latest AI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating closely with engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills through design deliverables, videos, and written artifacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a growth team driving user activation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about building collaborative relationships with many partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for turning complexity into usable, beautiful experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong design leader comfortable bringing your point of view to a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

