&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Partner closely with Stripe’s engineering organization to build the foundation of our early-stage university program&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Manage the full-cycle recruiting process for new graduate and intern candidates across multiple roles and offices&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Develop deep relationships with university groups, including faculty and student organizations, to design school-specific strategies that enhance our value proposition and brand on campus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Plan and execute on campus and virtual events with a focus on early engagement, education, and strategic branding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Screen candidates and ensure that our hiring process is consistent and inclusive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Drive a positive candidate experience for every new graduate and intern candidate considering a career at Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Build and iterate on our year-round internship program alongside teammates and cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Act as a resource to interns from hire to full-time conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Proactively share data-centric updates with internal stakeholders to maintain aligned decision making and build trusted partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A passion for building teams and delivering exceptional candidate experience for early talent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills with an appropriate blend of professionalism and friendliness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Proven abilities to create a strategic campus strategy and build a diverse pipeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;An active and data driven approach to problem solving, using data to identify trends and applying insights to drive efficient recruiting strategies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A growth mindset and is truly flexible, can shift tasks and priorities as circumstances change (At a fast-growing startup, they often do)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;An interest in working in a cross-functional and fluid environment, the ability to learn quickly, and welcome new perspectives&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability and willingness to travel up to 30% during peak recruiting cycles and work flexible hours as needed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A minimum of 3-4 years full-cycle university recruiting experience in a fast-paced, high-growth environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To further this important mission, we are building the foundation for a long-term talent bench at Stripe. We believe every campus hire can build products with meaningful impact at Stripe, and provide a far-reaching impact for anyone trying to grow their business online. We are looking for a University Recruiter to join our team to attract and hire the very best junior talent, while providing each candidate with an exceptional experience. This is a 12 month fixed term contract.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a small but mighty team, and are committed to big results. You will help shape the future of our early-stage programs and be responsible for all parts of the campus recruiting life cycle, including, but not limited to, organizing and leading on campus events, driving a strong and diverse candidate pipeline, branding, building relationships with internal stakeholders, and managing our global internship program. You must be a builder who thrives in a learning environment - unafraid to try new things, embrace new ideas, and welcome suggestions for how we can iterate on our processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Stripe’s engineering organization to build the foundation of our early-stage university program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full-cycle recruiting process for new graduate and intern candidates across multiple roles and offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop deep relationships with university groups, including faculty and student organizations, to design school-specific strategies that enhance our value proposition and brand on campus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute on campus events with a focus on early engagement, education, and strategic branding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screen candidates and ensure that our hiring process is consistent and inclusive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive a positive candidate experience for every new graduate and intern candidate considering a career at Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and iterate on our year-round internship program alongside teammates and cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a resource to interns from hire to full-time conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively share data-centric updates with internal stakeholders to maintain aligned decision making and build trusted partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A minimum of 5+ years full-cycle university recruiting experience in a fast-paced, high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A passion for building teams and delivering exceptional candidate experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with an appropriate blend of professionalism and friendliness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Proven abilities to create a strategic campus strategy and build a diverse pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;An active and data-driven approach to problem solving; you may enjoy making sense of the trends and using the insights to better your process to make it more efficient&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A growth mindset and truly flexible. You can shift tasks and priorities as circumstances change (At a fast-growing startup, they often do)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;An interest in working in a cross-functional and fluid environment, the ability to learn quickly, and no desire to take yourself too seriously (a wry sense of humor is always appreciated!)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability and willingness to travel up to 30% during peak recruiting cycles and work flexible hours as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow revenue, and create new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet. The work ahead is substantial, which gives you the opportunity to help put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing some of the most meaningful work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Early careers is a critical part of Stripe’s long-term talent strategy. The University Recruiting team helps shape the company we become by building the systems, programs, and hiring partnerships that bring exceptional interns, apprentices, and new graduates to Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As University Recruiting Manager, you will lead and develop a team of University Recruiters while owning the strategy and delivery of intern and new graduate hiring across Stripe. This is a high-visibility leadership role with a wide stage: you will work across every line of business and role type, partner with leaders throughout the company, and turn ambitious hiring goals into thoughtful, durable programs. You will also help lead Stripe’s global internship and apprenticeship programs, including onboarding, intern experience, and employee-relations escalations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;University Recruiting at Stripe is not a transactional recruiting function. This role goes well beyond attending a career fair or filling individual roles. You will set direction for an early careers strategy that supports Stripe’s business needs today and builds the talent pipeline we will need next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will bring strategic judgment, a builder’s mindset, and a deep commitment to craft. You will balance the operational rigor required to deliver at scale with the creativity to design programs and experiences that are clear, useful, and memorable. You will use data to understand what is working, where we are falling short, and what needs to change. And you will build credibility with leaders by making complex recruiting challenges easier to understand and act on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of full-cycle University Recruiters. Set a high bar for judgment, execution, and candidate and hiring-team partnership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver a clear early careers hiring strategy across Stripe’s lines of business and role families, translating business needs into practical recruiting plans and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders and hiring teams across the company to understand workforce needs, influence decisions, and meet ambitious hiring goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead global internship and apprenticeship programs, including onboarding, intern experience, program operations, and employee-relations escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve the end-to-end candidate experience in partnership with Finance, People Operations, Benefits, Onboarding, Legal, and other cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop thoughtful university, event, employer-brand, and employee-referral strategies that strengthen Stripe’s early careers talent pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use people analytics, recruiting data, and operational insights to identify patterns, measure performance, inform decisions, and improve the systems your team relies on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the bar for how University Recruiting works at Stripe by bringing rigor, care, and a strong point of view to both the strategy and the details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a strategic recruiting leader who sees early careers as a company-building function. You pair high standards with a practical work ethic, and you are comfortable moving from long-range planning to solving the immediate problem in front of you. You care about the quality of the work, the experience it creates for people, and the decisions behind it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ of recruiting experience, including designing and delivering a university recruiting strategy or major early talent initiative at a high-growth or complex organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of people management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven record of leading and developing University Recruiting professionals. You give clear feedback, build strong teams, and help people grow their judgment and capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic thinking and the ability to bring clarity to ambiguous, multi-stakeholder problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The communication and influencing skills to earn trust with leaders at every level and turn ideas into aligned action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high degree of ownership, a rigorous work ethic, and the ability to operate effectively in a fast-moving environment with shifting priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An appreciation for craft and beauty in the work. You care about the quality of the strategy, the programs, the candidate experience, and the operational details that make each of them work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep interest in people analytics, with experience using recruiting metrics, tools, and process data to improve decisions and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with hiring teams throughout the recruiting process as a trusted advisor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Financial Crimes Compliance Risk Oversight (FinCRO) team is looking for a U.S. Regulatory Compliance Lead for our Banking-as-a-Service (BaaS) business. You’ll own second-line oversight of Stripe’s U.S. BaaS products and bank-fintech partnerships. The work is practical and cross-functional: turn federal and state requirements and supervisory expectations into clear policies, controls, monitoring, evidence, and ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is focused on U.S. BaaS regulation. You’ll work across sponsor-bank and fintech responsibility mapping; BSA/AML and sanctions; consumer protection and fair lending; deposits and FDIC insurance representations; privacy, cybersecurity, incident response, and third-party risk; complaints and disputes; payment network and ACH rules; state money transmission and lending requirements; and regulatory exams, remediation, and change management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the second-line compliance framework for Stripe’s U.S. BaaS products (i.e., Capital, Issuing, and Treasury) and bank-fintech partnerships. Make sure responsibilities are clear across Stripe, sponsor banks, program managers, processors, and other partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn U.S. federal and state laws, guidance, enforcement actions, and supervisory expectations into practical policies, product requirements, controls, procedures, evidence standards, and monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and oversee controls for BSA/AML, customer identification and verification, customer due diligence and beneficial ownership, transaction monitoring, suspicious activity escalation, sanctions screening, and recordkeeping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee consumer and lending compliance for BaaS products, including UDAAP; Regulations E, Z, B, and DD; fair lending; FCRA; SCRA; FDCPA; complaints and disputes; adverse action; collections; marketing and disclosures; fees; account restrictions; and account closures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee deposit-product compliance, including FDIC insurance representations, Reg CC, pass-through insurance requirements, pooled or custodial structures, customer-level records, ledger integrity, reconciliation, and access to funds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define compliance expectations for privacy, cybersecurity, incident escalation, operational resilience, business continuity, data access, record retention, and an orderly wind-down of BaaS programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide second-line oversight on behalf of sponsor banks and other BaaS partners through risk assessments, due diligence, contract requirements, control testing, performance and complaint monitoring, issue management, and exit planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review new U.S. BaaS products and material changes. Identify applicable obligations, control gaps, licensing implications, and launch conditions, then drive remediation to closure with clear owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep pace with U.S. BaaS regulatory developments and enforcement trends, assess what they mean for Stripe, and coordinate timely changes with first-line teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help Stripe prepare for and respond to U.S. regulatory exams, supervisory engagements, audits, and formal commitments. Maintain defensible obligation mappings and evidence, identify gaps, and oversee remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product, Legal, Risk, Engineering, Operations, Internal Audit, sponsor-bank teams, and other specialists. Clarify ownership, challenge control design and execution, and give leaders a clear view of risk and progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 7 years of experience in U.S. banking, fintech, or financial-services compliance, including substantial work with BaaS, bank-fintech partnerships, embedded finance, or deposit, card, payment, or lending products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of the U.S. regulatory framework for BaaS and how responsibilities are divided among sponsor banks, fintechs, program managers, processors, and other service providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on expertise across several relevant areas, such as BSA/AML and sanctions, consumer financial protection, fair lending, deposit and FDIC insurance requirements, third-party risk, complaints and disputes, privacy and cybersecurity, ACH or card programs, and state money transmission or lending requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of turning complex U.S. legal and regulatory requirements into practical policies, product requirements, controls, procedures, monitoring, testing, and evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the full compliance control lifecycle: assessing risk and obligations, designing and implementing controls, documenting decisions, testing or monitoring, managing issues, overseeing remediation, and reporting to governance forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing new products and material changes, as well as supporting regulatory change, licensing analysis, exams, audits, enforcement remediation, or commitments to regulators and Boards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment, especially when ownership, regulatory precedent, or operating boundaries are not clear. You know how to separate second-line oversight from first-line execution and still move the work forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to influence and coordinate across Compliance, Legal, Product, Engineering, Risk, Operations, Internal Audit, sponsor banks, and senior stakeholders without relying on formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise writing and strong documentation skills. You can explain complex BaaS requirements and control decisions to technical, business, governance, partner-bank, and regulatory audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Escalations team offers a single point-of-entry for all user escalations raised by Stripes on behalf of a user. This team is accountable for all user escalation resolutions by either direct responsibility for resolution or by partnering with other support and non-support teams to facilitate a resolution. We aim to help users find speedy issue resolution and alleviate confusion and unnecessary effort from non-Support Stripes to do this. We will dig into specific user escalations to find top drivers for our most frequent and painful issues affecting our largest users as well as analyze the experience for the broader subset of users.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ultimately, these cases often shine a light on points of failure within Stripe, and the User Escalations team has the opportunity to create transformative user experiences, while also helping edit Stripe to rectify the structural issues that resulted in the escalation in the first place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high visibility, high impact role, with the responsibility to work with users and cross functional stakeholders, all while helping build this team from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will play a vital part in addressing user escalations at Stripe, focusing on swift and effective resolution. You’ll engage directly with users and the reporters of the escalations, while also collaborating with product and engineering teams to ensure user issues are resolved effectively. Additionally, you will leverage data and insights to identify trends, root causes and drive support&amp;nbsp; improvements across the wider organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to incoming User Escalations from Stripes in a timely manner (within agreed service levels) as well as triage, scope, and support to resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate directly with users to solve the most painful problems, via email and phone&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for timely and accurate resolution for all User Escalations within agreed service levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly, or in partnership with other Stripe teams, drive fast resolution and demonstrate extreme ownership in solving users issues completely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct thorough, data-driven root causes analyses of escalations, and work with partner teams to validate findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share findings and insights with leaders through forums and presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with partner teams to identify remediations to address root causes of escalations and drive change from a users’ first mentality&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge the status quo, identifying how and where Stripe needs to improve to better serve users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build the team and process from the ground up&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support training and socialization efforts for process adoption across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with partner teams and drive accountability for completion of remediations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand and help influence the relevant product roadmaps that will address the most frequent user escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5+ years of experience in a user support (customer facing) role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in troubleshooting and working on short SLA cases / escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience working on projects or process improvement initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and impeccable attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep sense of customer care and users-first perspective&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unflappable, exothermic energy under pressure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and a proven ability to create order out of chaos by building processes that help the team run better and deliver a better user experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid stakeholder management skills and an ability to influence others to drive progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sense of urgency and a drive to see issues through to resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading multiple concurrent projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical rigor and the ability to use data to inform decisions; comfort with SQL is a plus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in large / enterprise users is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive risk strategy for company-level strategic initiatives, which includes: partnering with the company’s product, legal, operations, sales, and partnerships teams to solve risk problems and ensure a positive user experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform research and analysis to assess Stripe’s current risk performance and develop and prioritize long-term strategic plans for future growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase business enablement, allowing the types of supportable merchants to safely grow at scale, continuously optimizing for efficiency and effectiveness, and stay hyper focused on a positive user experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge the status quo and provide multiple alternative solutions and key execution criteria.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute special projects and provide ad hoc analyses as initiatives, products, risks, and opportunities are constantly evolving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must have a Bachelor&#39;s Degree or foreign equivalent degree in Law, Business, Policy, Development Studies, or a related field, plus five (5) years post-bachelors, progressive related work experience as a Risk Strategist or a related occupation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must also have five (5) years of experience in each of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing risk strategies and solutions and working with technical products, including working with product and engineering, and operations teams for implementation;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distilling complex, ambiguous risk and policy problems into clear guidance for internal stakeholders and company users;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translating business requirements to technical configuration; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deriving insights from complex or technical problem spaces and evangelizing actionable product recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $161,637 - $204,000/yr.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions/sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hrs/week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;50% Telecommuting permitted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Up to 10% International and Domestic Travel Required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multiple Positions Available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional benefits for this role may include: equity, company bonus or sales commissions/bonuses; 401(k) plan; medical, dental, and vision benefits; and wellness stipends&lt;strong&gt;. NY79&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-DNI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research at Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s mission is to increase the GDP of the internet and expand economic access globally. We design tools and infrastructure to help our users start, run, and scale an online business from anywhere in the world. We believe there are too many barriers to doing business on the internet and that opportunities are not equally distributed around the world. We also believe that building and growing a business online is a problem rooted in code, language, and design, not finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That’s where you come in. We’re looking for an experienced UX Research Manager to join our growing UX Research team and help build, coach, and mentor a growing and highly skilled group of researchers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About UX research and the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UX Research team is part of Stripe’s Design team. It works across brand and product initiatives to deliver products and experiences that meet user needs. Since Stripe’s main audience is people who build products, we take pride in creating user-friendly, user-focused experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to conducting primary research, we enable other Stripes, including engineers, product managers, designers, and operations teams, to learn and apply research skills to global problems. You will help shape research as a core competency across Stripe and define how we put users first in our research.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a UX Research Manager, you will use your people-management and research expertise to lead a team of researchers that collaborates with product teams on core Payments and Risk products to build insight-driven product experiences. Core Payments includes Stripe’s in-person and online payment capabilities, checkout suite, Radar, and smart solutions that help businesses achieve optimal payment performance while balancing regulatory requirements, conversion, costs, and fraud considerations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Head of Research.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, manage, coach, and mentor a team of researchers conducting mixed-methods research throughout the product-development process for Stripe’s Payments and Risk product pillar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead initiatives and guide the research team through artificial intelligence (AI) transformation in its internal processes, how it conducts research for Stripe users, and how it supports the changing needs of product partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share research insights that deepen Stripe’s understanding of user needs and identify opportunities to meet those needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow the team to meet Stripe’s needs while developing individual contributors to deliver impactful, actionable research studies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Design and Stripe leadership to determine how to best use user research at Stripe and deepen our understanding of users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work as a strategic partner to business leads, product managers, design leaders, and Stripe leadership. Define long-term strategy and short-term tactics for products by grounding decisions in user needs and insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize research needs and approaches across multiple workstreams. Select the right project, scale, and scope at the right time, and deliver actionable insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable other Stripes to learn and apply research skills by building research programs, platforms, and toolkits that support tactical research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with other researchers to build Stripe’s research practice and infrastructure, including sourcing research vendors to support your team’s work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant user research experience working on digital experiences and generating actionable insights that drive impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of people-management and leadership experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience directly managing, coaching, and developing a team of user researchers, as well as recruiting and building research teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to set and achieve priorities that balance the needs of users, projects, the Research team, and Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting project work while mentoring and supporting a team of user researchers as they develop their craft and conduct research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant experience in financial technology, particularly payment processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to motivate and inspire people to do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting complex research at scale using a range of methods, including qualitative interviews, surveys, ideation sessions, ethnographic field research, usability evaluations, and diary studies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting primary research while mentoring and supporting a team of user researchers as they develop their craft and conduct research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including experience rolling out large-scale research programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A consistent focus on users and their needs, with experience driving impact from insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the balance between speed and rigor, and how research translates into design, product, and business decisions. Ability to work with urgency and focus while adapting methodological rigor to the situation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling research platforms, systems, or programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the Internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We cultivate a culture of collaboration, inclusivity, and support where every team member&#39;s voice matters. Our commitment shines through as we handle over a million support cases each year, empowering our users not just to solve problems but to achieve their goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe was built with simplicity in mind. We strive to deliver frictionless experiences for all of our users, whether they are an independent business, startup, SMB, or enterprise, and our mission is to provide all Stripe users with the best support experience possible. Today, Stripe handles over 1 million support cases per year and processes millions of internal transactions. We&#39;ll achieve excellence by thinking of support in a novel, solution-oriented way and viewing operations as an integral enabler of all our growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe has unique operational problems resulting from both our type of scale and the type of businesses we partner with as a result of &quot;growing the GDP of the Internet.&quot; Stripes leverage understanding of our products, the financial industry and money movement, and our processes to support both internal and external users. Doing so requires us to invest significant resources into building this experience ourselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe launched Stripe Delivery Centers—a global team to design, implement, and grow Stripe operations for the next decade. We are looking for dynamic and curious people who have a passion for solving global user issues, building operations, driving process improvement, and playing a front-line role in building this new operational capability for Stripe and accelerating growth. If you like challenging, scaled problems and are an amazing teammate, we want to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and solve external user issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze our processes and instigate changes to help scale our operations and improve user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with other Stripe teams to improve our product offerings and messaging around new products and features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain unique insights into how thousands of businesses on Stripe scale and operate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have an opportunity to learn how Stripe operates from the ground up and make a real impact on the future of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business process owners to run a critical workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a user-first mindset and are energized by the challenge of solving difficult problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have excellent communication skills, both written and verbal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You excel in analytical thinking and problem solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have prior experience in handling customer calls or offering services to internal and external users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy learning about technical products and processes. You are an organized self-starter with a passion for finding solutions to our users&#39; challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a process-oriented mindset and the ability to get things done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy working in an in-office environment with strong cross-team collaboration and support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to prioritize and enjoy working in a quick-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are humble and have a proven track record for working well across teams and with external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re willing to periodically work a weekend day for which you will receive a weekday off in lieu; the SDC operates in 9 hour shifts which are scheduled to fall between the hours of 12:30pm and 9:30pm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience or knowledge in user support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience working on projects or process improvement initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s People Systems team sits at the intersection of technology and human experience. We are internal consultants who turn ambiguity into scalable solutions. As part of the People Solutions organization, we partner with Corporate Technology, Finance, and the wider People team, including Talent and Total Rewards, to build a world-class employee experience. We are a strategy-first, quality-focused team that values technical rigor, adaptable problem-solving, and deep empathy for the Stripes we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Workday Analyst on the People Systems team, you’ll help administer and improve Stripe’s Workday environment. You’ll support the operational, cyclical, and change-management work that keeps our systems running reliably while building technical depth across key Workday domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work with People Systems teammates and cross-functional partners to turn well-defined requests into tested, documented system updates. You’ll own assigned workstreams with guidance and partner with senior teammates on complex changes, high-risk decisions, and system escalations. This role is well suited to someone who enjoys solving operational problems, working carefully with confidential data, and bringing clarity to Workday administration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and administer assigned Workday capabilities across defined functional areas, including Core Human Capital Management, Security, Time Tracking, Absence, and Reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete recurring operational work, including system queue monitoring, Workday Inbox support, account monitoring, access updates, routine data requests, compliance activities, and employee lifecycle processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support configuration and reporting requests through Enterprise Interface Builder loads, compensation range and grade profile updates, entity work, organizational changes, and related data maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct functional impact analyses, support daily change-management triage, and escalate complex or high-risk changes through established review paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test Workday releases, new features, configuration changes, and cyclical processes, then document results and implementation guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage Workday requests, gather requirements, clarify intended outcomes, resolve assigned issues, and partner with People team stakeholders on practical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain support documentation and knowledge content, identify recurring issues and system gaps, and contribute to improvements in processes and the employee experience while following applicable security, access, and audit requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of hands-on Workday configuration, administration, or human resources information system experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience configuring or supporting Workday Human Capital Management, Reporting, Security, Time Tracking, Absence, Payroll, or other employee lifecycle processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting data loads, reporting requests, system changes, testing, or operational workflows in an enterprise human resources information system environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with confidential information and business-critical processes with close attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to document work, partner with stakeholders, and raise risks or blockers when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with cross-functional teams on system or process improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Workday Enterprise Interface Builders, calculated fields, and advanced, matrix, or composite reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Workday releases, user acceptance testing, change management, or recurring People cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workday certification or relevant Workday training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in consulting or another role supporting internal or external clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace team’s mission is to create and support work environments that are welcoming, comfortable, and intuitive. These spaces are designed to promote collaboration, well-being, and productivity while adhering to the rigorous safety, security, and confidentiality standards required of a financial services company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace Experience team comprises hospitality-focused professionals who partner with the business to shape the daily experiences of Stripes, visitors, and candidates across 20+ global office locations. This geographically dispersed team oversees facilities management, daily operations, and local workplace programs, including events and onsites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a strategic leader and experienced manager with a high EQ who&#39;s enthusiastic about, and has a driving need to deliver, the best possible workplace experience for Stripes. You&#39;ll be a key member of our Experience team and responsible for ensuring that workplace operations, experiences, facilities, and programs run smoothly at our New York office. As a business partner, you have a deep understanding of the needs, experiences, and day-to-day realities of Stripes at your location and build strong relationships not only with site leads but also with cross-functional partners across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a high level of expertise and operational oversight—from understanding how the building functions top to bottom to governance of contractor team performance and ensuring financial accountability. A key part of the role is anticipating the needs of the business by understanding both the site and the broader context of company growth. You&#39;ll gather and synthesize feedback from multiple sources to ensure the workplace strategy is informed by real insights from the ground. While enterprise workplace strategy is developed centrally, you&#39;re expected to bring informed recommendations based on local business needs and operational insight, and to own successful implementation and adoption at your site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note this role requires an in office presence of 4 days per week.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee workplace operations at your site(s), providing direction on all workplace services, including building operations, front of house, shipping and receiving, events support, and employee health and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sound, independent operational decisions by balancing business impact, risk, cost, and employee experience, seeking alignment when decisions create broader organizational impact or precedent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and motivate a team of workplace services professionals, providing direction, coaching, and performance management to drive team excellence and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with internal stakeholders, including senior leadership, department heads, and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strong rapport with locally assigned Stripes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own operational performance for your site by monitoring service levels and utilization, identifying trends, resolving root causes, and driving continuous improvement across workplace operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively anticipate business needs by understanding both local context and company priorities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop thoughtful, data-informed recommendations that help shape workplace programs and experiences while maintaining alignment with global standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold workplace partners and service providers accountable for performance, ensuring contractual obligations, service levels, and operational standards are consistently achieved while driving continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with our Finance &amp;amp; Strategy partner and IFM partner to develop and oversee the opex budget for all facilities, opex, fixed assets, and events of the NYC office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the local site leadership team to activate the office by creating engagement, connection, and an inclusive environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft relevant communications and documentation regarding Workplace policies and programs for Stripes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent execution of global workplace programs, standards, and policies at your site,&amp;nbsp; as developed by our Food, Space Planning, and Programs teams, adapting implementation to local operational requirements while maintaining alignment with enterprise objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Workplace team&#39;s goals by taking on ad hoc tasks and projects as they arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in workplace/hospitality management in a fast-paced environment with a strong customer service orientation and an understanding of operational best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong demonstrated ability in facilities management, vendor, and budget management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strength in building relationships with key internal partners to ensure efficiency and understanding on cross-functional projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a team focused on customer service, hospitality, and operations, with the ability and desire to develop and coach your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to synthesize operational data, stakeholder feedback, and business context into clear recommendations that support sound decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Suite, Slack and Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear willingness to take a hands-on approach and dive into the details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence cross-functional partners and translate enterprise strategy into effective local execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently, digging into problems to understand the root cause and delivering scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive in a fast-paced workplace with rapidly changing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An innovative mindset with the ability to drive exceptional workplace services and operational improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace team’s mission is to create and support work environments that are welcoming, comfortable, and intuitive. These spaces are designed to promote collaboration, well-being, and productivity while adhering to the rigorous safety, security, and confidentiality standards required of a financial services company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace Experience team comprises operations, hospitality-focused and financially responsible professionals who directly shape the daily experiences of Stripes, visitors, and candidates across 20+ global office locations. This geographically dispersed team oversees facilities management, daily operations, and programs, including a culinary team dedicated to preparing nutritious meals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a strategic leader and experienced workplace manager with a high EQ who&#39;s enthusiastic about, and has a driving need to deliver, the best possible workplace experience for Stripes. You will be a key member of our Experience team and responsible for ensuring that workplace operations, experiences, facilities, and programs run smoothly at our Dublin office. As a business partner, you have a deep understanding of the needs, experiences, and day-to-day realities of Stripes at your location and build strong relationships not only with site leads but also with cross-functional partners across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a high level of expertise and operational oversight—from understanding how the building functions top to bottom to governance of contractor team performance and ensuring financial accountability. A key part of the role is anticipating the needs of the business by understanding both the site and the broader context of company growth. You will gather and synthesize feedback from multiple sources to ensure the workplace strategy is informed by real insights from the ground. While enterprise workplace strategy is developed centrally, you are expected to bring informed recommendations based on local business needs and operational insight, and to own successful implementation and adoption at your site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee workplace operations at your site(s), providing direction on all workplace services, including building operations, front of house, shipping &amp;amp; receiving, events support, and employee health and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sound, independent operational decisions by balancing business impact, risk, cost, and employee experience, seeking alignment when decisions create broader organizational impact or precedent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and motivate a team of workplace services professionals, providing direction, coaching, and performance management to drive team excellence and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with internal stakeholders, including senior leadership, department heads, and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strong rapport with locally assigned Stripes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own operational performance for your site by monitoring service levels and utilization, identifying trends, resolving root causes, and driving continuous improvement across workplace operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively anticipate business needs by understanding both local context and company priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop thoughtful, data-informed recommendations that help shape workplace programs and experiences while maintaining alignment with global standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold workplace partners and service providers accountable for performance, ensuring contractual obligations, service levels, and operational standards are consistently achieved while driving continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with our Finance &amp;amp; Strategy partner and IFM partner to develop and oversee the opex budget for all facilities, opex, fixed assets and events of the Dublin office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the local site leadership team to activate the office by creating engagement, connection, and an inclusive environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft relevant communications and documentation regarding Workplace policies and programs for Stripes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent execution of global workplace programs, standards, and policies at your site,&amp;nbsp; as developed by our Food, Space Planning, and Programs teams, adapting implementation to local operational requirements while maintaining alignment with enterprise objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Workplace team&#39;s goals by taking on ad hoc tasks and projects as they arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in workplace/hospitality management in a fast-paced environment with a strong customer service orientation and an understanding of operational best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong demonstrated ability in facilities management, vendor, and budget management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strength in building relationships with key internal partners to ensure efficiency and understanding on cross-functional projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a team focused on customer service, hospitality, and operations, with the ability and desire to develop and coach your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to synthesize operational data, stakeholder feedback, and business context into clear recommendations that support sound decision making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An innovative mindset with the ability to drive exceptional workplace services and operational improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Suite, Slack and Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear willingness to take a hands-on approach and dive into the details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence cross-functional partners and translate enterprise strategy into effective local execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently, digging into problems to understand the root cause and delivering scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive in a fast-paced workplace with rapidly changing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept at using and experimenting with provided AI tools for things like, identifying practical opportunities to automate routine work, generate operational insights from workplace data, and improve the experience for employees and visitors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An innovative mindset with the ability to drive exceptional workplace services and operational improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workplace Environments Project Manager (Europe, Middle East, and Africa)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Environments team is part of the Workplace organization at Stripe, within the broader Finance organization. The team combines expertise in project delivery, interior design, and space planning to create welcoming, functional spaces that balance operational integrity with craft, beauty, and moments of whimsy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team applies consistent global principles and high standards while responding to local culture, context, and user needs. The goal is to create workplaces that function intuitively, reflect Stripe, and help employees do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll shape and deliver workplaces across Europe, the Middle East, and Africa, leading projects that range from targeted improvements to complex fit-outs and major developments. You&#39;ll partner with regional and global teams to turn workplace strategy and standards into spaces that respond to local context and user needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires travel within Europe and occasional international travel based on project needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multiple workplace projects of varying sizes, complexity, and stages, with end-to-end accountability for scope, schedule, budget, risk, quality, and delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate global workplace strategy, design guidelines, and operational standards into locally effective project plans and outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish project governance, including decision rights, stakeholder checkpoints, escalation paths, risk management, and concise reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical due diligence and evaluate project constraints, delivery options, opportunities, and commercial trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Workplace Design, Space Planning, Workplace Operations, Real Estate, Finance and Strategy, Information Technology and Audio Visual, Security, Legal, and other regional and global teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select and manage external project managers, architects, engineers, contractors, furniture suppliers, and specialist consultants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure workplace designs function effectively and balance operational integrity with craft, beauty, and thoughtful moments of whimsy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience directly managing workplace, commercial construction, or office fit-out projects across Europe, the Middle East, and Africa or multiple international markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of construction delivery, including building services and mechanical, electrical, and plumbing systems, workplace technology, cost management, procurement, scheduling, and risk management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing multiple projects, budgets, priorities, and external partners while maintaining a high standard of delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating alignment across regional and global stakeholders, making informed decisions, challenging assumptions, and incorporating feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical artificial intelligence literacy, including the ability to identify appropriate uses, evaluate outputs critically, and use artificial intelligence responsibly to improve the quality or efficiency of your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as an in-house owner’s representative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reading and interpreting leases, work letters, landlord obligations, and related real estate documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Land-use or city-planning experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilities or workplace operations management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial kitchen and food-service programming, design, or construction experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering projects with sustainability, wellness, accessibility, or indoor environmental quality goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
